registerFaith({
  code:"uz",
  ui:{moreTitle:'Qoʻshimcha manbalar',libTitle:'Xudoni bilish',"start": "Boshlash", "next": "Keyingi", "prev": "Oldingi", "finish": "Tugatish", "allMoments": "Barcha lahzalar", "allMomentsEn": "all moments", "why": "Nega bu muhim", "whyEn": "why it matters", "play": "Butun hikoyani tinglang", "stop": "Toʻxtatish", "scriptLabel": "Oʻzbekcha", "done": "Barcha {t} lahza oʻqildi - barakalla!", "doneEn": "All {t} moments read - well done!", "prog": "{t} dan {n} taasi oʻqildi", "progEn": "{n} of {t} read", "soon": "Matn tez orada qoʻshiladi", "soonEn": "Content coming soon"},
  stories:[
  {id:'fgospel',kind:'solo',title:'The Gospel',ne:'Xushxabar',
sections:[
{id:'gospel',t:"The whole story in short",ne:"Xushxabar - qisqacha",art:FUZ_ART.ovstory,
paras:[
    ["Boshida Xudo yerni va undagi hamma narsani yaratdi. Soʻng U insonni Oʻz surati va siyratida yaratdi - munosabat uchun, sevgi uchun.", "Boshida Khudo yerni va undagi hamma narsani yaratdi. Sawng U insonni Awz surati va siyratida yaratdi - munosabat uchun, sevgi uchun.", "In the beginning God created the earth and everything in it. And he made human beings in his own image — for relationship, for love.", "Genesis 1:26–27"],
    ["Inson bilan Xudo doʻst edilar. Ammo insonlar Xudoga qarshi isyon yoʻlini tanladilar - va oʻsha isyon bizni Undan ajratib qoʻydi.", "Inson bilan Khudo dawst edilar. Ammo insonlar Khudoga qarshi isyon yawlini tanladilar - va awsha isyon bizni Undan ajratib qawydi.", "Humanity and God shared friendship. But human beings chose the road of rebellion against God — and that rebellion separated us from him.", "Genesis 3"],
    ["Isyon yoʻlini tanlagan biz edik - shunga qaramay Xudo bizni shu qadar sevdiki, buzilgan munosabatni davolab, uni yana qoʻshish uchun reja tuzdi.", "Isyon yawlini tanlagan biz edik - shunga qaramay Khudo bizni shu qadar sevdiki, buzilgan munosabatni davolab, uni yana qawshish uchun reja tuzdi.", "We were the ones who chose to rebel — yet God loved us so much that he made a plan to heal that broken relationship and join it back together.", "Genesis 3:15"],
    ["Shunday qilib Xudo bitta xalqni tanladi - Isroilni. U Ibrohim ismli oddiy bir odamdan boshlandi, va Xudo unga vaʼda berdi: sen orqali yer yuzidagi barcha xalqlar baraka topadi. Shu xalq orqali Xudo butun dunyoga shifo va najot keltiradi.", "Shunday qilib Khudo bitta khalqni tanladi - Isroilni. U Ibrohim ismli oddiy bir odamdan boshlandi, va Khudo unga vada berdi: sen orqali yer yuzidagi barcha khalqlar baraka topadi. Shu khalq orqali Khudo butun dunyoga shifo va najot keltiradi.", "So God chose one nation — Israel. It began with a single ordinary man named Abraham, and God promised him: through you, all the peoples of the earth will be blessed. Through this nation God would bring healing and salvation to the whole world.", "Genesis 12:1–3"],
    ["Chunki yuzlab yillar oʻtib, aynan oʻsha xalqdan Iso keldi. U bokira qizdan tugʻildi; U Xudoning Oʻgʻlidir. U bizni isyonimizdan qutqarish va Xudo bilan munosabatimizni davolash uchun keldi.", "Chunki yuzlab yillar awtib, aynan awsha khalqdan Iso keldi. U bokira qizdan tughildi; U Khudoning Awghlidir. U bizni isyonimizdan qutqarish va Khudo bilan munosabatimizni davolash uchun keldi.", "Because hundreds of years later, from that very nation, Jesus came. He was born of a virgin; he is the Son of God. He came to save us from our rebellion and to heal our relationship with God.", "Matthew 1:18–23 · Luke 19:10"],
    ["Bu shunday boʻldi: Iso gunohlarimiz uchun qurbonlik sifatida xochda jon berdi. Uchinchi kuni esa oʻlimdan tirildi - biz insonlarni tutib turgan zulmatning oʻzini yengib.", "Bu shunday bawldi: Iso gunohlarimiz uchun qurbonlik sifatida khochda jon berdi. Uchinchi kuni esa awlimdan tirildi - biz insonlarni tutib turgan zulmatning awzini yengib.", "It happened like this: Jesus died on the cross as the sacrifice for our sins. And on the third day he rose from the dead — overcoming the very darkness we humans were trapped in.", "1 Corinthians 15:3–4"],
    ["Bugun Iso tirik, Xudoning oʻng tomonida oʻtiribdi. Unga imon keltirib, Uning ortidan yurgan har bir kishi Xudoning oilasiga - Xudoning oʻz farzandi sifatida - uyiga qaytariladi.", "Bugun Iso tirik, Khudoning awng tomonida awtiribdi. Unga imon keltirib, Uning ortidan yurgan har bir kishi Khudoning oilasiga - Khudoning awz farzandi sifatida - uyiga qaytariladi.", "Today Jesus is alive, seated at the right hand of God. And whoever believes in him and follows him is brought home into God’s family — as God’s own child.", "Hebrews 12:2 · John 1:12"],
    ["Imon keltirganlarga Xudo Oʻzining Muqaddas Ruhini beradi - Xudoning Oʻzi ichimizga makon qilib, bizni tasalli berib, har kuni yoʻl koʻrsatadi.", "Imon keltirganlarga Khudo Awzining Muqaddas Ruhini beradi - Khudoning Awzi ichimizga makon qilib, bizni tasalli berib, har kuni yawl kawrsatadi.", "To those who believe, God gives his Holy Spirit — God himself making his home within us, comforting us and guiding us day by day.", "John 14:16–17"],
    ["Va bir kun Iso yana keladi. U hamma narsani yangilaydi - koʻz yoshi ham, oʻlim ham qolmaydi - va Xudo Oʻz xalqi bilan abadiy yashaydi.", "Va bir kun Iso yana keladi. U hamma narsani yangilaydi - kawz yoshi ham, awlim ham qolmaydi - va Khudo Awz khalqi bilan abadiy yashaydi.", "And one day Jesus will come again. He will make all things new — no more tears, no more death — and God will dwell with his people forever.", "Revelation 21:1–4"],
    ["Bu xabar unga ishongan har bir kishiga shifo va tiklanish keltiradi - u biz bilan Xudo orasidagi doʻstlikni qaytarib beradi. Xushxabar shudir: biz ishlab topadigan narsa emas, balki Xudo beradigan sovgʻa.", "Bu khabar unga ishongan har bir kishiga shifo va tiklanish keltiradi - u biz bilan Khudo orasidagi dawstlikni qaytarib beradi. Khushkhabar shudir: biz ishlab topadigan narsa emas, balki Khudo beradigan sovgha.", "This message brings healing and restoration to everyone who believes it — it gives back the fellowship between us and God. This is the gospel: not something we earn, but a gift God gives.", "Romans 1:16 · Ephesians 2:8–9"],
    ["Bu - Xudoning insoniyat uchun rejasi va U butun dunyoga najotni qanday keltirgani haqidagi umumiy koʻrinish. Bundan keyin biz oʻsha hikoyani boshidan - har bir lahzani batafsil - koʻrib chiqamiz.", "Bu - Khudoning insoniyat uchun rejasi va U butun dunyoga najotni qanday keltirgani haqidagi umumiy kawrinish. Bundan keyin biz awsha hikoyani boshidan - har bir lahzani batafsil - kawrib chiqamiz.", "This is an overview of God’s plan for humanity, and how he brought salvation to the whole world. From here, we will walk through the same story from the beginning — one moment at a time, in detail."]]}]},
  {id:"fstory",kind:'arc',title:"God’s Story",ne:"Xudoning hikoyasi",
   sections:[
   {id:"creation",t:"In the beginning",ne:"Boshida",art:FUZ_ART.creation,
    note:["Xudoga biz kerak emas edik - U bizni istadi. Inson oʻz Yaratuvchisi bilan doʻstlik uchun yaratilgan, va hikoya oʻsha doʻstlik butun boʻlgan yaxshi dunyoda ochiladi.", "Khudoga biz kerak emas edik - U bizni istadi. Inson awz Yaratuvchisi bilan dawstlik uchun yaratilgan, va hikoya awsha dawstlik butun bawlgan yakhshi dunyoda ochiladi.", "God did not need us — he wanted us. Human beings were made for friendship with their Maker, and the story opens in a good world where that friendship is whole."],
    paras:[["Boshida Xudo osmon va yerni yaratdi. U yaratgan hamma narsa yaxshi edi.", "Boshida Khudo osmon va yerni yaratdi. U yaratgan hamma narsa yakhshi edi.", "In the beginning God made the heavens and the earth. Everything he made was good.", "Genesis 1"],["Xudo insonni Oʻz surati va siyratida yaratdi - erkak va ayol qilib.", "Khudo insonni Awz surati va siyratida yaratdi - erkak va ayol qilib.", "God made human beings in his own image — male and female.", "Genesis 1:27"],["Uning suratida yaratilgan boʻlish chuqur maʼnoga ega edi: inson butun borliqqa Xudoning fe.lini va tabiatini aks ettirishi kerak edi. U yaratgan boshqa hamma narsadan farqli oʻlaroq, biz Uning oʻxshashi boʻlishimiz uchun yaratilganmiz.", "Uning suratida yaratilgan bawlish chuqur manoga ega edi: inson butun borliqqa Khudoning felini va tabiatini aks ettirishi kerak edi. U yaratgan boshqa hamma narsadan farqli awlaroq, biz Uning awkhshashi bawlishimiz uchun yaratilganmiz.", "And being made in his image meant something deep: humans were to reflect the character and nature of God to the whole creation. Unlike the rest of what he made, we were made to be his likeness.", "Genesis 1:26–28"],["Xudo insonlarga aytdi: koʻpayinglar va bu yerga gʻamxoʻrlik qilinglar.", "Khudo insonlarga aytdi: kawpayinglar va bu yerga ghamkhawrlik qilinglar.", "God told the humans: be fruitful, and take care of this earth.", "Genesis 1:28 · 2:15"],["Insonlar Xudo bilan birga Adan degan bogʻda yashadilar. U ular bilan oʻsha yerda yurar edi - uzilmagan munosabat, inson bilan Xudo orasidagi shirin doʻstlik.", "Insonlar Khudo bilan birga Adan degan boghda yashadilar. U ular bilan awsha yerda yurar edi - uzilmagan munosabat, inson bilan Khudo orasidagi shirin dawstlik.", "The humans dwelt with God in a garden called Eden. He would walk with them there — an unbroken relationship, sweet fellowship between humanity and God.", "Genesis 2:8 · 3:8"],["Bogʻning oʻrtasida bitta daraxt turardi, va Xudo aytdi: uning mevasini yemanglar - yesangiz, oʻlasiz. Chunki sevadigan Xudo bizga doim tanlov qoldiradi: biz U bilan munosabatni istaymizmi yoki yoʻqmi? Bu tanlov bizniki.", "Boghning awrtasida bitta darakht turardi, va Khudo aytdi: uning mevasini yemanglar - yesangiz, awlasiz. Chunki sevadigan Khudo bizga doim tanlov qoldiradi: biz U bilan munosabatni istaymizmi yoki yawqmi? Bu tanlov bizniki.", "In the middle of the garden stood one tree, and God said: do not eat its fruit — if you eat it, you will die. Because the God who loves always leaves us a choice: do we want relationship with him, or not? That choice is ours to make.", "Genesis 2:16–17"],["Xudo Oʻzi yaratgan hamma narsaga qaradi va aytdi: bu juda yaxshi. Yettinchi kuni esa U dam oldi.", "Khudo Awzi yaratgan hamma narsaga qaradi va aytdi: bu juda yakhshi. Yettinchi kuni esa U dam oldi.", "God looked at all he had made and said: it is very good. And on the seventh day he rested.", "Genesis 1:31 · 2:2–3"]]},
   {id:"fall",t:"The break",ne:"Uzilish",art:FUZ_ART.fall,
    note:["Xudoning yoʻllarini rad etganlar insonlarning oʻzi edi - shunga qaramay Xudo ularni qutqarish rejasini tuzdi.", "Khudoning yawllarini rad etganlar insonlarning awzi edi - shunga qaramay Khudo ularni qutqarish rejasini tuzdi.", "Even though it was humans who rejected God’s ways, God still made a plan to save them."],
    paras:[["Oʻsha birinchi insonlarning ismi Odam va Momo Havo edi. Ammo bir kuni oʻsha yaxshi bogʻga ilon kirib keldi - va u yolgʻon gapirdi. Afsuski, Odam va Momo Havo Xudoning soʻzini qoʻyib yuborib, ilonga ishondilar - va mevani yedilar.", "Awsha birinchi insonlarning ismi Odam va Momo Havo edi. Ammo bir kuni awsha yakhshi boghga ilon kirib keldi - va u yolghon gapirdi. Afsuski, Odam va Momo Havo Khudoning sawzini qawyib yuborib, ilonga ishondilar - va mevani yedilar.", "The names of those first humans were Adam and Eve. But one day, into that good garden, came a serpent — and it told a lie. Sadly, Adam and Eve let go of God’s word and believed the snake instead — and they ate the fruit.", "Genesis 3:1–6"],["Yolgʻon shunday edi: bu mevani ye, va sen Xudoday boʻlasan. Xudoga ishonib boʻlmaydi - U sendan yaxshi narsalarni ayamoqda.", "Yolghon shunday edi: bu mevani ye, va sen Khudoday bawlasan. Khudoga ishonib bawlmaydi - U sendan yakhshi narsalarni ayamoqda.", "The lie went like this: eat this fruit, and you will become like God. God cannot be trusted — he is withholding good things from you.", "Genesis 3:4–5"],["Yeganlari zahoti qalblarini aybdorlik va uyat toʻldirdi - va ular yashirindilar. Birinchi marta insonlar Xudodan qoʻrqdilar.", "Yeganlari zahoti qalblarini aybdorlik va uyat tawldirdi - va ular yashirindilar. Birinchi marta insonlar Khudodan qawrqdilar.", "The moment they ate, guilt and shame flooded their hearts — and they hid. For the first time, humans were afraid of God.", "Genesis 3:7–10"],["Shunga qaramay Xudo ularni qidirib keldi va soʻradi: qayerdasan? Va Oʻz qoʻllari bilan ularni kiyintirdi.", "Shunga qaramay Khudo ularni qidirib keldi va sawradi: qayerdasan? Va Awz qawllari bilan ularni kiyintirdi.", "Yet God came looking for them and asked: where are you? And with his own hands he clothed them.", "Genesis 3:9 · 3:21"],["Xudo nima boʻlganini soʻraganda, Odam Momo Havoni aybladi, Momo Havo esa ilonni aybladi. Gunoh bizni bir-birimizdan ham uzoqlashtiradi.", "Khudo nima bawlganini sawraganda, Odam Momo Havoni aybladi, Momo Havo esa ilonni aybladi. Gunoh bizni bir-birimizdan ham uzoqlashtiradi.", "When God asked what had happened, Adam blamed Eve, and Eve blamed the serpent. Sin pushes us apart from one another too.", "Genesis 3:12–13"],["Xudoning amridan yuz oʻgirish - gunoh shudir. Va gunoh inson bilan Xudo orasidagi doʻstlikni uzdi.", "Khudoning amridan yuz awgirish - gunoh shudir. Va gunoh inson bilan Khudo orasidagi dawstlikni uzdi.", "Turning from God’s command — that is sin. And sin broke the fellowship between humanity and God.", "Genesis 3:8–10"],["Xudo aytgan narsa, afsuski, sodir boʻldi. U ularga Adandan chiqishni aytdi - va oʻsha kundan buyon inson bilan Xudo orasida ajralish bor. Shunga qaramay U vaʼda berdi: bir kuni Qutqaruvchi keladi.", "Khudo aytgan narsa, afsuski, sodir bawldi. U ularga Adandan chiqishni aytdi - va awsha kundan buyon inson bilan Khudo orasida ajralish bor. Shunga qaramay U vada berdi: bir kuni Qutqaruvchi keladi.", "What God had said would happen, sadly happened. He told them to leave Eden — and from that day there has been a separation between humanity and God. Yet he gave a promise: one day a Rescuer would come.", "Genesis 3:15"]]},
   {id:"spread",t:"Sin spreads",ne:"Gunoh tarqaldi",art:FUZ_ART.spread,
    note:["Gunoh hech qachon bitta odamda toʻxtab qolmaydi - u oilalarga va butun jamiyatlarga tarqaladi. Ammo yovuzlik ortib borganda ham Xudo inoyat bilan ish qilaverdi - U Nuhning oilasini saqlab qoldi va dunyoga yangi boshlanish berdi.", "Gunoh hech qachon bitta odamda tawkhtab qolmaydi - u oilalarga va butun jamiyatlarga tarqaladi. Ammo yovuzlik ortib borganda ham Khudo inoyat bilan ish qilaverdi - U Nuhning oilasini saqlab qoldi va dunyoga yangi boshlanish berdi.", "Sin never stays with one person — it spreads through families and whole societies. Yet even as evil grew, God kept acting in grace: he preserved Noah’s family and gave the world a fresh start."],
    paras:[["Gunoh butun dunyoga tarqaldi, va inson qalbi Xudodan uzoqlashib ketdi.", "Gunoh butun dunyoga tarqaldi, va inson qalbi Khudodan uzoqlashib ketdi.", "Sin spread through the whole world, and the human heart drifted far from God.", "Genesis 4–6"],["Bu bogʻdan tashqaridagi eng birinchi oilada koʻrindi: katta aka Qobil hasadga toʻlib, oʻz ukasi Hobilni oʻldirdi. Hikoyadagi birinchi oʻlim qotillik edi.", "Bu boghdan tashqaridagi eng birinchi oilada kawrindi: katta aka Qobil hasadga tawlib, awz ukasi Hobilni awldirdi. Hikoyadagi birinchi awlim qotillik edi.", "It showed in the very first family outside the garden: the elder brother, Cain, filled with envy, killed his own brother Abel. The first death in the story was a murder.", "Genesis 4:8"],["Xudo insoniyatning yovuzligini koʻrganda, Uning yuragi qaygʻurdi.", "Khudo insoniyatning yovuzligini kawrganda, Uning yuragi qayghurdi.", "When God saw the evil of humanity, his heart was grieved.", "Genesis 6:5–6"],["Dunyo shunday zoʻravonlikka toʻldiki, Xudo uni buyuk toʻfon bilan yuvishga qaror qildi. Ammo bitta sodiq odam bor edi - Nuh. Xudo unga juda katta kema qurdirdi.", "Dunyo shunday zawravonlikka tawldiki, Khudo uni buyuk tawfon bilan yuvishga qaror qildi. Ammo bitta sodiq odam bor edi - Nuh. Khudo unga juda katta kema qurdirdi.", "The world filled with such violence that God resolved to wash it clean with a great flood. But there was one faithful man — Noah. God had him build an enormous boat.", "Genesis 6:11–14"],["Shunday boʻlsa ham, Xudo dunyoni tashlab qoʻymadi. U Nuhga va uning oilasiga inoyat koʻrsatdi.", "Shunday bawlsa ham, Khudo dunyoni tashlab qawymadi. U Nuhga va uning oilasiga inoyat kawrsatdi.", "Even so, God did not abandon the world. He showed grace to Noah and his family.", "Genesis 6–9"],["Nuh orqali Xudo dunyoga yangi boshlanish berdi - toʻgʻri yashashi kerak boʻlgan yangi inson oilasi. Ammo inson qalbi oʻshaligicha qoldi. Gunoh yana tarqala boshladi - yolgʻiz yangi boshlanishning oʻzi yetarli emas edi.", "Nuh orqali Khudo dunyoga yangi boshlanish berdi - tawghri yashashi kerak bawlgan yangi inson oilasi. Ammo inson qalbi awshaligicha qoldi. Gunoh yana tarqala boshladi - yolghiz yangi boshlanishning awzi yetarli emas edi.", "Through Noah God gave the world a fresh start — a new human family meant to live rightly. But the human heart stayed the same. Sin began to spread again — a fresh start alone was not enough.", "Genesis 9:20–21 · 11"],["Ancha keyin odamlar bir joyga toʻplanib, osmonga yetadigan minora qura boshladilar - Xudosiz buyuk boʻlish uchun. U joyning nomi Bobil edi.", "Ancha keyin odamlar bir joyga tawplanib, osmonga yetadigan minora qura boshladilar - Khudosiz buyuk bawlish uchun. U joyning nomi Bobil edi.", "Much later, people gathered in one place and began building a tower to reach the sky — to become great without God. The place was called Babel.", "Genesis 11:1–4"],["Bobilda odamlar oʻz nomlarini ulugʻlamoqchi boʻldilar. Ammo Xudoning rejasi oldinga siljib bordi.", "Bobilda odamlar awz nomlarini ulughlamoqchi bawldilar. Ammo Khudoning rejasi oldinga siljib bordi.", "At Babel people tried to make their own name great. But God’s plan kept moving forward.", "Genesis 11"],["Xudo ularning hammasini turli tillarda gapiradigan qildi - va xalqlar butun yer yuziga tarqalib ketdi.", "Khudo ularning hammasini turli tillarda gapiradigan qildi - va khalqlar butun yer yuziga tarqalib ketdi.", "God made them all speak different languages — and so the people scattered across the whole earth.", "Genesis 11:8–9"]]},
   {id:"abraham",t:"A promise to Abraham",ne:"Ibrohimga vaʼda",art:FUZ_ART.abraham,
    note:["Xudoning buzilgan dunyoga javobi, ajablanarli tarzda, bitta oddiy oiladir. Ibrohim orqali BARCHA xalqlar baraka topadi degan vaʼda Xushxabar boshlanadigan joydir - va u Oʻzbekistonga ham yetib keladi.", "Khudoning buzilgan dunyoga javobi, ajablanarli tarzda, bitta oddiy oiladir. Ibrohim orqali BARCHA khalqlar baraka topadi degan vada Khushkhabar boshlanadigan joydir - va u Awzbekistonga ham yetib keladi.", "God’s answer to a broken world is, surprisingly, one ordinary family. The promise that ALL nations would be blessed through Abraham is where the good news begins — and it reaches Uzbekistan too."],
    paras:[["Oʻsha tarqalgan xalqlar orasidan - Nuhning oʻz naslidan - Xudo bitta odamni tanladi: Ibrohimni, Ur degan shahardan chiqqan oddiy odamni.", "Awsha tarqalgan khalqlar orasidan - Nuhning awz naslidan - Khudo bitta odamni tanladi: Ibrohimni, Ur degan shahardan chiqqan oddiy odamni.", "From among those scattered peoples — from the line of Noah himself — God chose one man: Abraham, an ordinary man from a city called Ur.", "Genesis 11:31 · 12:1"],["Xudo Ibrohimni chaqirdi: sening oilang orqali yer yuzidagi barcha xalqlar baraka topadi.", "Khudo Ibrohimni chaqirdi: sening oilang orqali yer yuzidagi barcha khalqlar baraka topadi.", "God called Abraham: through your family, all the peoples of the earth will be blessed.", "Genesis 12:1–3"],["Nega Xudo Ibrohimni tanladi? Boshqalardan koʻra solihroq boʻlgani uchun emas. Xudo rahmga boy, va U insoniyatni qutqarishni istadi. Biz Unga bizni tashlab ketish uchun har qanday sabab bergan edik - shunga qaramay buyuk sevgisi va saxovati tufayli U bunday qilmadi.", "Nega Khudo Ibrohimni tanladi? Boshqalardan kawra solihroq bawlgani uchun emas. Khudo rahmga boy, va U insoniyatni qutqarishni istadi. Biz Unga bizni tashlab ketish uchun har qanday sabab bergan edik - shunga qaramay buyuk sevgisi va sakhovati tufayli U bunday qilmadi.", "Why did God choose Abraham? Not because he was more righteous than others. God is rich in mercy, and he wanted to save humanity. We had given him every reason to abandon us — yet because of his great love and generosity, he did not.", "Ephesians 2:4 · Deuteronomy 7:7–8"],["Ibrohim qayerga ketayotganini ham bilmay, uyini va yurtini tashlab chiqdi. Imon shunday yurishdir.", "Ibrohim qayerga ketayotganini ham bilmay, uyini va yurtini tashlab chiqdi. Imon shunday yurishdir.", "Abraham left his home and his country without even knowing where he was going. That walk is what faith looks like.", "Hebrews 11:8"],["Bir kechasi Xudo uni tashqariga olib chiqib aytdi: yuqoriga qara va yulduzlarni sanay olsang, sana. Nasling ham shuncha koʻp boʻladi.", "Bir kechasi Khudo uni tashqariga olib chiqib aytdi: yuqoriga qara va yulduzlarni sanay olsang, sana. Nasling ham shuncha kawp bawladi.", "One night God led him outside and said: look up and count the stars — if you can. That is how many your descendants will be.", "Genesis 15:5"],["Ibrohim Xudoga ishondi - va Xudo uni solih deb hisobladi.", "Ibrohim Khudoga ishondi - va Khudo uni solih deb hisobladi.", "Abraham trusted God — and God counted him as righteous.", "Genesis 15:6"],["Ammo bir muammo bor edi: Ibrohim va uning xotini Soraxonim keksa edilar, va ularning umuman farzandi yoʻq edi. Vaʼda imkonsiz tuyulardi. Shunga qaramay aynan oʻz vaqtida Soraxonim oʻgʻil tugʻdi - Isʼhoq, ismining maʼnosi kulgi. Maʼlum boʻldiki, Xudo uchun imkonsiz narsa yoʻq.", "Ammo bir muammo bor edi: Ibrohim va uning khotini Sorakhonim keksa edilar, va ularning umuman farzandi yawq edi. Vada imkonsiz tuyulardi. Shunga qaramay aynan awz vaqtida Sorakhonim awghil tughdi - Ishoq, ismining manosi kulgi. Malum bawldiki, Khudo uchun imkonsiz narsa yawq.", "But there was a problem: Abraham and his wife Sarah were old, and they had no child at all. The promise sounded impossible. Yet at just the right time Sarah bore a son — Isaac, whose name means laughter. Nothing, it turned out, is impossible for God.", "Genesis 18:10–14 · 21:1–6"],["Shu bitta oiladan Xudoning qutqarish hikoyasi oldinga siljidi.", "Shu bitta oiladan Khudoning qutqarish hikoyasi oldinga siljidi.", "From this one family, God’s rescue story moved forward.", "Genesis 12–50"]]},
   {id:"exodus",t:"Rescue from Egypt",ne:"Misrdan qutqarilish",art:FUZ_ART.exodus,
    note:["Isroil kuchli boʻlgani uchun ozod boʻlmadi - Xudo Ibrohimning oilasiga bergan vaʼdasini bajardi. U eshitadi, U ish qiladi - va hech bir saltanat Uning yoʻlida tura olmaydi.", "Isroil kuchli bawlgani uchun ozod bawlmadi - Khudo Ibrohimning oilasiga bergan vadasini bajardi. U eshitadi, U ish qiladi - va hech bir saltanat Uning yawlida tura olmaydi.", "Israel did not walk free because they were strong — God kept the promise he had made to Abraham’s family. He hears, he acts, and no empire can stand in his way."],
    paras:[["Vaqt oʻtishi bilan Ibrohimning oilasi buyuk xalqqa aylandi - Isroil deb atalgan xalqqa. Ammo ular Misr degan yurtga borib qoldilar, va uning shohi ularni qul qildi. Toʻrt yuz yil ular azob chekdilar. Ular Xudoga faryod qildilar - va U eshitdi.", "Vaqt awtishi bilan Ibrohimning oilasi buyuk khalqqa aylandi - Isroil deb atalgan khalqqa. Ammo ular Misr degan yurtga borib qoldilar, va uning shohi ularni qul qildi. Tawrt yuz yil ular azob chekdilar. Ular Khudoga faryod qildilar - va U eshitdi.", "As time passed, Abraham’s family grew into a great people — a people called Israel. But they ended up in a country called Egypt, and its king made them slaves. For four hundred years they suffered. They cried out to God — and he heard.", "Exodus 1 · 2:23–25"],["Xudo Oʻz xalqining azobini koʻrdi va ularni Misrdan olib chiqish uchun Muso ismli odamni yubordi.", "Khudo Awz khalqining azobini kawrdi va ularni Misrdan olib chiqish uchun Muso ismli odamni yubordi.", "God saw the suffering of his people, and he sent a man named Moses to lead them out of Egypt.", "Exodus 3"],["Misr shohi isroilliklarni qoʻyib yuborishdan bosh tortdi. Ammo koʻplab moʻjizalar va alomatlar orqali Xudo uni ularni ozod qilishga majbur etdi.", "Misr shohi isroilliklarni qawyib yuborishdan bosh tortdi. Ammo kawplab mawjizalar va alomatlar orqali Khudo uni ularni ozod qilishga majbur etdi.", "The king of Egypt refused to let the Israelites go. But through many wonders and miracles God forced him to set them free.", "Exodus 7–12"],["Oʻsha moʻjizalar va alomatlar barcha xalqlarga koʻrsatdi: Xudo har qanday saltanatdan kuchliroqdir.", "Awsha mawjizalar va alomatlar barcha khalqlarga kawrsatdi: Khudo har qanday saltanatdan kuchliroqdir.", "Those wonders and miracles showed all the nations that God is more powerful than any empire.", "Exodus 9:16"],["Xudo ular bilan ahd bogʻladi va kelib Oʻz xalqining oʻrtasida makon qildi.", "Khudo ular bilan ahd boghladi va kelib Awz khalqining awrtasida makon qildi.", "God made a covenant with them and came to dwell right among his people.", "Exodus 19–40"],["Ahd oddiy vaʼda emas - bu ikki tarafni birlashtiradigan chuqur va mustahkam ahdlashuv, nikohga oʻxshaydi. Xudo aytdi: Men sizning Xudoyingiz boʻlaman, siz esa Mening xalqim boʻlasiz. Va U ularga butun hayot tarzi uchun yoʻl-yoʻriq ham berdi.", "Ahd oddiy vada emas - bu ikki tarafni birlashtiradigan chuqur va mustahkam ahdlashuv, nikohga awkhshaydi. Khudo aytdi: Men sizning Khudoyingiz bawlaman, siz esa Mening khalqim bawlasiz. Va U ularga butun hayot tarzi uchun yawl-yawriq ham berdi.", "A covenant is no casual promise — it is a deep, binding pledge that joins two parties, like a marriage. God said: I will be your God, and you will be my people. And he gave them guidance for their whole way of life.", "Exodus 6:7 · 19–20"],["Va Xudo sodiq edi - ular Uning ortidan yurganlarida, U ularga kerak boʻlgan hamma narsani taʼminlab berdi.", "Va Khudo sodiq edi - ular Uning ortidan yurganlarida, U ularga kerak bawlgan hamma narsani taminlab berdi.", "And God was faithful: as they followed him, he provided everything they needed.", "Exodus 16–17"],
["Ammo Xudo shunchalik buyuk sadoqat va rahm-shafqat koʻrsatgan boʻlsa ham, Isroil qayta-qayta isyon qilish va Uning yetakchiligini rad etish yoʻlini tanladi. Shunday qilib oʻsha aylanish davom etdi: gunoh, Xudoning hukmi va tarbiyasi, xalqning tavbasi - va ularni yana qabul qiladigan Xudoning rahm-shafqati.", "Ammo Khudo shunchalik buyuk sadoqat va rahm-shafqat kawrsatgan bawlsa ham, Isroil qayta-qayta isyon qilish va Uning yetakchiligini rad etish yawlini tanladi. Shunday qilib awsha aylanish davom etdi: gunoh, Khudoning hukmi va tarbiyasi, khalqning tavbasi - va ularni yana qabul qiladigan Khudoning rahm-shafqati.", "Yet even though God showed such radical faithfulness and mercy, Israel still chose again and again to rebel and reject his leadership. So the same cycle kept turning: sin, God’s judgment and discipline, the people’s repentance — and God’s mercy receiving them back.", "Exodus 32 · Numbers 14"],["Muso qirq yil Isroilga yetakchilik qildi. Undan keyin Yoshua ismli rahbar xalqqa yetakchilik qila boshladi.", "Muso qirq yil Isroilga yetakchilik qildi. Undan keyin Yoshua ismli rahbar khalqqa yetakchilik qila boshladi.", "Moses led Israel for forty years. After him, a leader named Joshua began to lead the people.", "Deuteronomy 34 · Joshua 1"]]},
   {id:"kings",t:"Kings and prophets",ne:"Shohlar va paygʻambarlar",art:FUZ_ART.kings,
    note:["Har bir shoh muvaffaqiyatsizlikka uchraydi - va gap aynan shunda. Hikoya bizga shohligi hech qachon tugamaydigan yaxshiroq Shohni orziqib kutishni oʻrgatmoqda.", "Har bir shoh muvaffaqiyatsizlikka uchraydi - va gap aynan shunda. Hikoya bizga shohligi hech qachon tugamaydigan yakhshiroq Shohni orziqib kutishni awrgatmoqda.", "Every king fails — and that is the point. The story is training us to long for a better King, whose kingdom never ends."],
    paras:[["Misrdan keyin Xudo Isroilni Oʻzi vaʼda qilgan yurtga olib keldi. Ular oʻsha yerda joylashdilar - va vaqt oʻtib aytdilar: bizga ham shoh ber, boshqa barcha xalqlarda boʻlgani kabi.", "Misrdan keyin Khudo Isroilni Awzi vada qilgan yurtga olib keldi. Ular awsha yerda joylashdilar - va vaqt awtib aytdilar: bizga ham shoh ber, boshqa barcha khalqlarda bawlgani kabi.", "After Egypt, God brought Israel into the land he had promised. There they settled — and in time they said: give us a king, like all the other nations have.", "Joshua · 1 Samuel 8"],["Isroil shohlari orasida eng sevimlisi Dovud ismli odam edi. Shoh boʻlishidan oldin u shunchaki yosh choʻpon bola edi - ammo Xudo uni tanladi, chunki U Dovudda Oʻz yuragiga mos odamni koʻrdi.", "Isroil shohlari orasida eng sevimlisi Dovud ismli odam edi. Shoh bawlishidan oldin u shunchaki yosh chawpon bola edi - ammo Khudo uni tanladi, chunki U Dovudda Awz yuragiga mos odamni kawrdi.", "The best-loved of Israel’s kings was a man named David. Before he was king he was only a young shepherd boy — but God chose him, because he saw in David a man after his own heart.", "1 Samuel 13:14 · 16:7"],["Goliyot ismli devqomat dushman jangchisi Isroilga qarshi chiqdi - ammo Xudo yosh Dovudga uni yengish uchun kuch berdi, va Isroil dushmanlari ustidan gʻalaba koʻrdi.", "Goliyot ismli devqomat dushman jangchisi Isroilga qarshi chiqdi - ammo Khudo yosh Dovudga uni yengish uchun kuch berdi, va Isroil dushmanlari ustidan ghalaba kawrdi.", "A giant enemy warrior named Goliath defied Israel — but God empowered young David to defeat him, and Israel saw victory over their enemies.", "1 Samuel 17"],["Xudo Dovudni shoh qildi va vaʼda berdi: sening naslingdan shohligi hech qachon tugamaydigan Shoh chiqadi.", "Khudo Dovudni shoh qildi va vada berdi: sening naslingdan shohligi hech qachon tugamaydigan Shoh chiqadi.", "God made David king and promised: from your line will come a King whose kingdom never ends.", "2 Samuel 7"],["Dovuddan keyin yuzlab yillar davomida koʻp shohlar Isroilni boshqardi. Bir nechtasi yaxshi edi - ammo koʻpchiligi chuqur gunohda yashadi. Ular soxta xudolarga sigʻindilar, kambagʻallarni ezdilar, va xalqni Xudodan uzoqlashtirdilar.", "Dovuddan keyin yuzlab yillar davomida kawp shohlar Isroilni boshqardi. Bir nechtasi yakhshi edi - ammo kawpchiligi chuqur gunohda yashadi. Ular sokhta khudolarga sighindilar, kambaghallarni ezdilar, va khalqni Khudodan uzoqlashtirdilar.", "After David, many kings ruled Israel over hundreds of years. A few were good — but most lived in deep sin. They worshiped false gods, crushed the poor, and led the people far from God.", "1–2 Kings"],["Bu yurakni ezadigan aylanma edi. Bir muddat xalq Xudo bilan yurardi; keyin asta-sekin murosaga borib soxta xudolarga burilardi; bu ularni dushmanlari zulmiga olib borardi; azobda ular Xudoga faryod qilardilar - va U ularni qutqarardi. Soʻng, biroz vaqtdan keyin, oʻsha aylanma yana boshlanardi.", "Bu yurakni ezadigan aylanma edi. Bir muddat khalq Khudo bilan yurardi; keyin asta-sekin murosaga borib sokhta khudolarga burilardi; bu ularni dushmanlari zulmiga olib borardi; azobda ular Khudoga faryod qilardilar - va U ularni qutqarardi. Sawng, biroz vaqtdan keyin, awsha aylanma yana boshlanardi.", "It was a heartbreaking cycle. For a while the people would walk with God; then slowly they would compromise and turn to false gods; that led them into oppression under their enemies; in their misery they would cry out to God — and he would save them. And then, after a while, the same circle would begin again.", "Judges 2:11–19"],["Va oʻsha shohlarning butun yillari davomida Xudo paygʻambarlar yuborib turdi - shohlarga va xalqqa Oʻz soʻzlarini aytish uchun Xudo tanlagan odamlarni. Ular ogohlantirish keltirdilar - gunohdan qayting, Xudoga qayting - va umid ham keltirdilar.", "Va awsha shohlarning butun yillari davomida Khudo payghambarlar yuborib turdi - shohlarga va khalqqa Awz sawzlarini aytish uchun Khudo tanlagan odamlarni. Ular ogohlantirish keltirdilar - gunohdan qayting, Khudoga qayting - va umid ham keltirdilar.", "And all through the years of those kings, God kept sending prophets — people God chose to speak his words to the kings and to the people. They brought warning — turn from sin, come back to God — and they brought hope.", "2 Kings 17:13"],["Paygʻambarlar umid haqida ham gapirdilar. Ular aytdilar: bir kun Xudo Oʻz xalqi bilan yangi ahd tuzadi, va ularning gunohi toʻliq kechiriladi. Va ular keladigan Xudoning Xizmatkori haqida ham aytdilar - U xalqning gunohini Oʻz zimmasiga olib, ularning oʻrniga koʻtaradi.", "Payghambarlar umid haqida ham gapirdilar. Ular aytdilar: bir kun Khudo Awz khalqi bilan yangi ahd tuzadi, va ularning gunohi tawliq kechiriladi. Va ular keladigan Khudoning Khizmatkori haqida ham aytdilar - U khalqning gunohini Awz zimmasiga olib, ularning awrniga kawtaradi.", "The prophets also spoke of hope. One day, they said, God would make a new covenant with his people, and their sin would be fully forgiven. And they told of a coming Servant of God who would take the people’s sin upon himself and carry it in their place.", "Jeremiah 31 · Isaiah 53"],["Paygʻambarlar orqali Xudo vaʼda berdi: Men sizga yangi yurak beraman, va ichingizga Oʻz Ruhimni solaman.", "Payghambarlar orqali Khudo vada berdi: Men sizga yangi yurak beraman, va ichingizga Awz Ruhimni solaman.", "Through the prophets God promised: I will give you a new heart, and I will put my own Spirit within you.", "Ezekiel 36:26–27"],["Ammo shohlarning va xalqning koʻpchiligi eshitmadi. Oxir-oqibat gunoh oʻz mevasini berdi: dushman qoʻshini yurtni bosib oldi, va Isroil xalqi oʻz yurtini tashlab ketishga majbur boʻldi. Bu Xudoning tarbiyasi edi - paygʻambarlar yillar davomida ogohlantirgan tarbiya.", "Ammo shohlarning va khalqning kawpchiligi eshitmadi. Okhir-oqibat gunoh awz mevasini berdi: dushman qawshini yurtni bosib oldi, va Isroil khalqi awz yurtini tashlab ketishga majbur bawldi. Bu Khudoning tarbiyasi edi - payghambarlar yillar davomida ogohlantirgan tarbiya.", "But most of the kings and the people would not listen. In the end sin bore its fruit: an enemy army conquered the land, and the people of Israel were forced to leave their own country. This was God’s discipline — the discipline the prophets had warned about for years.", "2 Kings 17 · 25"]]},
   {id:"wait",t:"The long wait",ne:"Uzoq kutish",art:FUZ_ART.wait,
    note:["Bizning zaifligimiz va bevafoligimiz Xudoning sodiqligini bekor qilmaydi. Oʻsha toʻrt yuz jim yil davomida ham U sodiq qoldi - tarixdagi eng buyuk kelishga tayyorgarlik koʻrib.", "Bizning zaifligimiz va bevafoligimiz Khudoning sodiqligini bekor qilmaydi. Awsha tawrt yuz jim yil davomida ham U sodiq qoldi - tarikhdagi eng buyuk kelishga tayyorgarlik kawrib.", "Our weakness and unfaithfulness do not cancel God’s faithfulness. Through four hundred quiet years he stayed faithful — preparing the greatest arrival in history."],
    paras:[["Shunday qilib paygʻambarlarning ogohlantirishi amalga oshdi: Isroil xalqi oʻz yurtidan uzoqqa olib ketildi. Ularning uylari va dalalari ortda qoldi. Butun umid yoʻqolganday koʻrinardi.", "Shunday qilib payghambarlarning ogohlantirishi amalga oshdi: Isroil khalqi awz yurtidan uzoqqa olib ketildi. Ularning uylari va dalalari ortda qoldi. Butun umid yawqolganday kawrinardi.", "So the prophets’ warning came true: the people of Israel were carried far from their own land. Their homes and their fields were left behind. It looked as if all hope was lost.", "2 Kings 25"],["Bu surgun deb ataladi: Bobil qoʻshinlari Quddusni vayron qildilar, Xudoning maʼbadini yoqdilar, va xalqni asir qilib oʻz yurtlariga olib ketdilar.", "Bu surgun deb ataladi: Bobil qawshinlari Quddusni vayron qildilar, Khudoning mabadini yoqdilar, va khalqni asir qilib awz yurtlariga olib ketdilar.", "This is called the exile: the armies of Babylon tore down Jerusalem, burned God’s temple, and carried the people away captive to Babylon.", "2 Kings 25:8–11"],["Ular surgunda boʻlganlarida ham Xudo ularni tashlab qoʻymadi - ular bunga loyiq boʻlgani uchun emas, balki Xudo behad rahmdil boʻlgani va U hamon butun yer yuziga najot keltirishga sodiq qolgani uchun.", "Ular surgunda bawlganlarida ham Khudo ularni tashlab qawymadi - ular bunga loyiq bawlgani uchun emas, balki Khudo behad rahmdil bawlgani va U hamon butun yer yuziga najot keltirishga sodiq qolgani uchun.", "While they were in exile, God did not abandon them — not because they deserved it, but because God is radically merciful, and he was still committed to bringing salvation to the whole earth.", "Jeremiah 29:10–14"],["Tarix bir narsani ochiq koʻrsatdi: biz insonlar oʻz kuchimiz bilan Xudoga sodiq qola olmas edik - isyonimiz qayta-qayta takrorlanardi. Bizga boshqacha javob kerak edi. Va paygʻambarlar orqali Xudo aynan shuni vaʼda qildi: Men sizdan tosh yurakni olib, goʻsht yurak beraman, va qonunimni yuragingizning oʻziga yozaman.", "Tarikh bir narsani ochiq kawrsatdi: biz insonlar awz kuchimiz bilan Khudoga sodiq qola olmas edik - isyonimiz qayta-qayta takrorlanardi. Bizga boshqacha javob kerak edi. Va payghambarlar orqali Khudo aynan shuni vada qildi: Men sizdan tosh yurakni olib, gawsht yurak beraman, va qonunimni yuragingizning awziga yozaman.", "History had made one thing plain: we humans could not stay faithful to God in our own strength — our rebellion kept repeating. We needed a different answer. And through the prophets God promised exactly that: I will take out your heart of stone and give you a heart of flesh, and I will write my law on your very hearts.", "Ezekiel 36:26 · Jeremiah 31:33"],["Hizqiyol paygʻambar bir vahiy koʻrdi: quruq suyaklarga toʻla vodiy. Xudo undan soʻradi - bu suyaklar yana tirila oladimi? Soʻng Xudoning Oʻz nafasi oʻsha suyaklarni hayot bilan toʻldirdi, va katta bir olomon oyoqqa turdi. Belgi aniq edi: oʻlganday boʻlgan yurakni ham Xudo qayta tiriltira oladi.", "Hizqiyol payghambar bir vahiy kawrdi: quruq suyaklarga tawla vodiy. Khudo undan sawradi - bu suyaklar yana tirila oladimi? Sawng Khudoning Awz nafasi awsha suyaklarni hayot bilan tawldirdi, va katta bir olomon oyoqqa turdi. Belgi aniq edi: awlganday bawlgan yurakni ham Khudo qayta tiriltira oladi.", "The prophet Ezekiel saw a vision: a valley full of dry bones. God asked him — can these bones live again? Then God’s own breath filled those bones with life, and a great multitude stood up. The sign was clear: even a heart as good as dead, God can bring back to life.", "Ezekiel 37:1–10"],["Surgunga olib ketilganlar orasida Doniyor ismli yigit bor edi. Oʻsha begona yurtda, hatto ibodat taqiqlanganda ham, u kuniga uch marta derazasini ochib ibodat qilishda davom etdi. Uni sherlar uyasiga tashlashganda ham Xudo uni omon saqladi.", "Surgunga olib ketilganlar orasida Doniyor ismli yigit bor edi. Awsha begona yurtda, hatto ibodat taqiqlanganda ham, u kuniga uch marta derazasini ochib ibodat qilishda davom etdi. Uni sherlar uyasiga tashlashganda ham Khudo uni omon saqladi.", "Among those carried into exile was a young man named Daniel. In that foreign land, even when prayer was outlawed, he kept opening his window to pray three times a day. Even when he was thrown into a den of lions, God kept him safe.", "Daniel 6"],["Yetmish yildan keyin, aynan vaʼda qilinganday, Xudo ularni oʻz yurtlariga qaytardi. Ular Quddus shahrini va maʼbadni qayta qurdilar. Ammo qalbining tubida hamma bilardi: eng buyuk vaʼda hali bajarilmagan edi.", "Yetmish yildan keyin, aynan vada qilinganday, Khudo ularni awz yurtlariga qaytardi. Ular Quddus shahrini va mabadni qayta qurdilar. Ammo qalbining tubida hamma bilardi: eng buyuk vada hali bajarilmagan edi.", "Seventy years later, just as promised, God brought them back to their own land. They rebuilt the city of Jerusalem and the temple. But deep down everyone knew: the greatest promise had not yet been kept.", "Ezra · Nehemiah"],["Shunda ham ular kutdilar: vaʼda qilingan Qutqaruvchi - Masih - qachon keladi?", "Shunda ham ular kutdilar: vada qilingan Qutqaruvchi - Masih - qachon keladi?", "Still they waited: when would the promised Rescuer — the Messiah — come?", "Isaiah 9:6–7"],["Ammo bu qanday sodir boʻlishini hech kim bilmasdi. Isroilda koʻpchilik ularni zolimlardan ozod qiladigan jangchini kutardi. Haqiqiy javob ancha chuqurroq edi - ularni gunohlaridan ozod qiladigan qutqaruvchi. Xudo Oʻzi maʼbadiga qaytardi - va insonlarning hayoti va ozodligi uchun Oʻz jonini berardi.", "Ammo bu qanday sodir bawlishini hech kim bilmasdi. Isroilda kawpchilik ularni zolimlardan ozod qiladigan jangchini kutardi. Haqiqiy javob ancha chuqurroq edi - ularni gunohlaridan ozod qiladigan qutqaruvchi. Khudo Awzi mabadiga qaytardi - va insonlarning hayoti va ozodligi uchun Awz jonini berardi.", "But nobody knew how it would happen. Many in Israel waited for a warrior who would deliver them from their oppressors. The true answer ran far deeper — a deliverer who would free them from their sins. God himself would return to his temple — and lay down his own life for the life and freedom of human beings.", "Malachi 3:1 · Mark 10:45"],["Toʻrt yuz yil davomida sukunat. Ammo Xudo vaʼdasini unutmagan edi.", "Tawrt yuz yil davomida sukunat. Ammo Khudo vadasini unutmagan edi.", "For four hundred years, silence. But God had not forgotten his promise.", "Malachi → Matthew"]]},
   {id:"immanuel",t:"God with us",ne:"Xudo biz bilan",art:FUZ_ART.immanuel,
    note:["Yaratuvchi Oʻz yaratganining ichiga qadam qoʻydi. Isoda Xudo uzoqdan yordam yubormadi - U Oʻzi keldi.", "Yaratuvchi Awz yaratganining ichiga qadam qawydi. Isoda Khudo uzoqdan yordam yubormadi - U Awzi keldi.", "The Creator stepped inside his own creation. In Jesus, God did not send help from a distance — he came himself."],
    paras:[["Va shundan keyin - oʻsha uzoq, jim kutishdan soʻng - Iso tugʻildi. Unga yana bir ism ham berildi: Immanuil, maʼnosi Xudo biz bilan.", "Va shundan keyin - awsha uzoq, jim kutishdan sawng - Iso tughildi. Unga yana bir ism ham berildi: Immanuil, manosi Khudo biz bilan.", "And then — after that long, silent wait — Jesus was born. He was given another name too: Immanuel, which means God with us.", "Matthew 1:23"],["Uning tugʻilishidan ancha oldin paygʻambarlar yozgan edilar: biz uchun bola tugʻiladi, va U Ajoyib Maslahatchi, Qudratli Xudo, Abadiyat Otasi, Tinchlik Shahzodasi deb ataladi. Yana yozilgan ediki, U bokira qizdan tugʻiladi - va aynan shunday boʻldi.", "Uning tughilishidan ancha oldin payghambarlar yozgan edilar: biz uchun bola tughiladi, va U Ajoyib Maslahatchi, Qudratli Khudo, Abadiyat Otasi, Tinchlik Shahzodasi deb ataladi. Yana yozilgan ediki, U bokira qizdan tughiladi - va aynan shunday bawldi.", "Long before his birth the prophets had written: for us a child will be born, and he will be called Wonderful Counselor, Mighty God, Everlasting Father, Prince of Peace. It was also written that he would be born of a virgin — and that is exactly what happened.", "Isaiah 9:6 · 7:14"],["Xudo Oʻzi inson boʻldi va oramizda makon qildi.", "Khudo Awzi inson bawldi va oramizda makon qildi.", "God himself became human and made his home among us.", "John 1:14"],["Iso Xudo kim ekanini va qandayligini mukammal ochib berdi. U koʻp nomlar bilan tanilgan - Xudoning Kalomi, inson boʻlgan Xudo, Xudoning Oʻgʻli. Oʻzi esa koʻpincha Inson Oʻgʻli nomini ishlatgan - bu nom Doniyor paygʻambarning vahiysidan olingan, u yerda har bir xalq va tildagi odamlar Unga xizmat qiladi.", "Iso Khudo kim ekanini va qandayligini mukammal ochib berdi. U kawp nomlar bilan tanilgan - Khudoning Kalomi, inson bawlgan Khudo, Khudoning Awghli. Awzi esa kawpincha Inson Awghli nomini ishlatgan - bu nom Doniyor payghambarning vahiysidan olingan, u yerda har bir khalq va tildagi odamlar Unga khizmat qiladi.", "Jesus revealed perfectly who God is and what God is like. He is known by many names — the Word of God, God become flesh, the Son of God. And he himself most often used the name Son of Man — a name from the prophet Daniel’s vision, where people of every nation and language serve him.", "John 1:1,14 · Daniel 7:13–14"],["Iso saroyda emas, balki Nosira degan kichik qishloqda oʻsdi. U ishladi, charchoqni bildi, koʻz yoshini bildi - U hayotimizni ichidan tushunadi.", "Iso saroyda emas, balki Nosira degan kichik qishloqda awsdi. U ishladi, charchoqni bildi, kawz yoshini bildi - U hayotimizni ichidan tushunadi.", "Jesus grew up not in a palace but in a small village called Nazareth. He worked, knew tiredness, knew tears — he understands our life from the inside.", "Luke 2:39–52 · Hebrews 4:15"],["Iso Xudoning Shohligi haqidagi Xushxabarni eʼlon qildi va yoʻqolganlarni qidirib chiqdi.", "Iso Khudoning Shohligi haqidagi Khushkhabarni elon qildi va yawqolganlarni qidirib chiqdi.", "Jesus announced the good news of God’s kingdom and went looking for the lost.", "Luke 4 · Luke 19:10"],["Yahyo ismli bir paygʻambar bor edi, uni Xudo xalqni tayyorlash uchun yuborgan. Yahyo Isoni koʻrganda baqirdi: qaranglar - Xudoning Qoʻzisi, dunyoning gunohini olib ketuvchi!", "Yahyo ismli bir payghambar bor edi, uni Khudo khalqni tayyorlash uchun yuborgan. Yahyo Isoni kawrganda baqirdi: qaranglar - Khudoning Qawzisi, dunyoning gunohini olib ketuvchi!", "There was a prophet named John, sent by God to make the people ready. When John saw Jesus, he cried out: look — the Lamb of God, who takes away the sin of the world!", "John 1:29"]]},
   {id:"crossgs",t:"The cross and the empty tomb",ne:"Xoch va boʻsh qabr",art:FUZ_ART.cross,
    note:["Isoning oʻlimi va tirilishi bizga shifo topib, Xudo bilan doʻstlikka qaytarilish imkonini berdi.", "Isoning awlimi va tirilishi bizga shifo topib, Khudo bilan dawstlikka qaytarilish imkonini berdi.", "Jesus’ death and resurrection made it possible for us to be healed and restored back into fellowship with God."],
    paras:[["Xochdan oldingi kechada Iso bir bogʻda ibodat qildi. U kelayotgan azob-uqubatni bilar edi va iltijo qildi: Ota, boshqa yoʻl boʻlsa, bu kosani Mendan olib qoʻy - ammo Mening irodam emas, Sening irodang bajo boʻlsin. Uning jonini hech kim olmadi - sevgi tufayli U bu yoʻlni oʻz ixtiyori bilan tanladi.", "Khochdan oldingi kechada Iso bir boghda ibodat qildi. U kelayotgan azob-uqubatni bilar edi va iltijo qildi: Ota, boshqa yawl bawlsa, bu kosani Mendan olib qawy - ammo Mening irodam emas, Sening irodang bajo bawlsin. Uning jonini hech kim olmadi - sevgi tufayli U bu yawlni awz ikhtiyori bilan tanladi.", "The night before the cross, Jesus prayed in a garden. He knew the suffering that was coming, and he asked: Father, if there is another way, take this cup from me — yet not my will, but yours be done. No one took his life from him; he chose that road willingly, out of love.", "Luke 22:39–44 · John 10:18"],["Ertasi kuni U hibsga olindi va qatl etildi - oʻsha davrning eng shafqatsiz jazosi boʻlgan xochga mixlandi. Shunga qaramay bularning hammasi Xudoning rejasi ichida edi.", "Ertasi kuni U hibsga olindi va qatl etildi - awsha davrning eng shafqatsiz jazosi bawlgan khochga mikhlandi. Shunga qaramay bularning hammasi Khudoning rejasi ichida edi.", "The next day he was arrested and executed — nailed to a cross, the cruelest punishment of that age. Yet all of it lay inside God’s plan.", "Luke 23 · Acts 2:23"],["Xochda Iso bizning gunohimizni Oʻz zimmasiga oldi.", "Khochda Iso bizning gunohimizni Awz zimmasiga oldi.", "On the cross Jesus took our sin upon himself.", "Isaiah 53"],["Iso jon berganda maʼbadning pardasi yuqoridan pastgacha yirtildi. Oʻsha parda xalqni Xudoning huzuridan ajratib turardi - uning ichkarisiga faqat oliy ruhoniy kira olardi, u ham yilda faqat bir marta. Endi Xudoning huzuriga boradigan yoʻl hamma uchun ochiq.", "Iso jon berganda mabadning pardasi yuqoridan pastgacha yirtildi. Awsha parda khalqni Khudoning huzuridan ajratib turardi - uning ichkarisiga faqat oliy ruhoniy kira olardi, u ham yilda faqat bir marta. Endi Khudoning huzuriga boradigan yawl hamma uchun ochiq.", "When Jesus died, the temple curtain tore from top to bottom. That curtain had separated the people from God’s presence — only the highest priest could go behind it, and only once a year. Now the way into God’s presence stands open to everyone.", "Matthew 27:51 · Hebrews 9:7"],["Uchinchi kuni Iso oʻlimdan tirildi. Oʻlimning oʻzi yengildi.", "Uchinchi kuni Iso awlimdan tirildi. Awlimning awzi yengildi.", "On the third day Jesus rose from the dead. Death itself was defeated.", "Luke 24"],["Oʻsha yerda U insoniyatni changalida tutib turgan qorongʻu kuchlarni ham yengdi. Na biz, na ular tushunmagan edik: xoch boshidanoq reja edi. U biz uchun yana ozodlikda va Xudo bilan munosabatda yurish yoʻlini ochib berdi.", "Awsha yerda U insoniyatni changalida tutib turgan qoronghu kuchlarni ham yengdi. Na biz, na ular tushunmagan edik: khoch boshidanoq reja edi. U biz uchun yana ozodlikda va Khudo bilan munosabatda yurish yawlini ochib berdi.", "There he also defeated the dark powers that held humanity in their grip. Neither we nor they had understood: the cross was the plan from the very beginning. It opened the way for us to walk in freedom and relationship with God once again.", "Colossians 2:15 · 1 Corinthians 2:8"],["Endi Xudoga qaytish yoʻli ochiq. Uzilgan doʻstlik yana qoʻshildi.", "Endi Khudoga qaytish yawli ochiq. Uzilgan dawstlik yana qawshildi.", "Now the way back to God stands open. The broken fellowship is joined again.", "Romans 5:1–11"],["Uning oʻz gunohi yoʻq edi - shunga qaramay U bizningkini koʻtardi, toki biz Xudo oldida solih turaylik. Bu buyuk almashuvdir.", "Uning awz gunohi yawq edi - shunga qaramay U bizningkini kawtardi, toki biz Khudo oldida solih turaylik. Bu buyuk almashuvdir.", "He had no sin of his own — yet he carried ours, so that we could stand righteous before God. This is the great exchange.", "2 Corinthians 5:21"]]},
   {id:"newcreation",t:"New creation",ne:"Yangi yaratilish",art:FUZ_ART.newcreation,
    
    paras:[["Tirilganidan keyin Iso shogirdlariga - Uning ortidan yurgan doʻstlariga - Muqaddas Ruhni berdi va ularni butun dunyoga yubordi.", "Tirilganidan keyin Iso shogirdlariga - Uning ortidan yurgan dawstlariga - Muqaddas Ruhni berdi va ularni butun dunyoga yubordi.", "After he rose, Jesus gave his disciples — the friends who followed him — the Holy Spirit, and sent them out into all the world.", "Acts 1–2"],["Muqaddas Ruh Xudoning Oʻzidir - endi U Oʻz xalqining ichida makon qilib, ularga tasalli berib, yoʻl koʻrsatadi.", "Muqaddas Ruh Khudoning Awzidir - endi U Awz khalqining ichida makon qilib, ularga tasalli berib, yawl kawrsatadi.", "The Holy Spirit is God himself — now making his home inside his people, comforting them and guiding the way.", "John 14:16–17"],["Ilgari odamlar Xudo bilan uchrashish uchun maʼbadga borar edilar. Endi hayratlanarli narsa yuz berdi: Xudoning Oʻz xalqi, Uning Ruhi bilan toʻlgan holda, Uning maʼbadidir. Biz Unga sigʻinish va bir-birimizni sevish uchun yigʻilganimizda, Xudo ichimizda va oramizda yashaydi.", "Ilgari odamlar Khudo bilan uchrashish uchun mabadga borar edilar. Endi hayratlanarli narsa yuz berdi: Khudoning Awz khalqi, Uning Ruhi bilan tawlgan holda, Uning mabadidir. Biz Unga sighinish va bir-birimizni sevish uchun yighilganimizda, Khudo ichimizda va oramizda yashaydi.", "Before, people went to a temple to meet God. Now something astonishing has happened: God’s own people, filled with his Spirit, ARE his temple. As we gather to worship him and love one another, God dwells within us and among us.", "1 Corinthians 3:16"],["Birinchi imonlilar hayotni birga yashadilar - birga ovqatlanib, ibodat qilib, bir-biriga yordam berib. Ularning bir-biriga boʻlgan sevgisi qarab turgan dunyoga koʻrsatdi: bu yerda boshqacha bir narsa boʻlmoqda.", "Birinchi imonlilar hayotni birga yashadilar - birga ovqatlanib, ibodat qilib, bir-biriga yordam berib. Ularning bir-biriga bawlgan sevgisi qarab turgan dunyoga kawrsatdi: bu yerda boshqacha bir narsa bawlmoqda.", "The first believers lived life together — eating, praying, helping one another. The love they had for one another showed the watching world that something different was happening.", "Acts 2:42–47"],["Va taklif Isroil bilan tugamadi - endi barcha xalqlar Xudoning xalqi boʻlishga chaqirilgan. Osiyolik, afrikalik, gʻarblik - har bir xalq va tildagi odamlar bitta oilada, birga Isoning ortidan yurib, sadoqat, sevgi va itoat hayotida. Isoning hayoti, oʻlimi va tirilishi dunyoni oʻzgartirdi - bittadan odamni, har birini sodiq, mehribon va saxiy Yaratuvchi bilan munosabatga qaytarib.", "Va taklif Isroil bilan tugamadi - endi barcha khalqlar Khudoning khalqi bawlishga chaqirilgan. Osiyolik, afrikalik, gharblik - har bir khalq va tildagi odamlar bitta oilada, birga Isoning ortidan yurib, sadoqat, sevgi va itoat hayotida. Isoning hayoti, awlimi va tirilishi dunyoni awzgartirdi - bittadan odamni, har birini sodiq, mehribon va sakhiy Yaratuvchi bilan munosabatga qaytarib.", "And the invitation did not stop at Israel — now all nations are called to become the people of God. Asian, African, Western — people of every nation and language in one family, following Jesus together in a life of devotion, love and obedience. The life, death and resurrection of Jesus changed the world — one person at a time, each one brought back into relationship with a faithful, kind and generous Creator.", "Galatians 3:28 · Revelation 7:9"],
["Oʻsha Xushxabar butun dunyoga tarqalgan. Bugun Oʻzbekistonda baʼzi odamlar Isoning ortidan yuradi - ammo koʻpchilik hali ham yurmaydi. Shuning uchun Xudo Oʻz Xushxabarini eʼlon qilish uchun Oʻzbekistonga odamlar yuborishda davom etmoqda. Hikoya hamon yozilmoqda.", "Awsha Khushkhabar butun dunyoga tarqalgan. Bugun Awzbekistonda bazi odamlar Isoning ortidan yuradi - ammo kawpchilik hali ham yurmaydi. Shuning uchun Khudo Awz Khushkhabarini elon qilish uchun Awzbekistonga odamlar yuborishda davom etmoqda. Hikoya hamon yozilmoqda.", "That good news has spread across the world. In Uzbekistan some people follow Jesus today — yet most still do not. So God keeps sending people to Uzbekistan to proclaim his good news. The story is still being written.", "Acts 1:8"],["Bir kun Iso yana keladi, va Xudo yangi osmon va yangi yer yaratadi.", "Bir kun Iso yana keladi, va Khudo yangi osmon va yangi yer yaratadi.", "One day Jesus will come again, and God will make a new heaven and a new earth.", "Revelation 21:1"],["U yerda Xudo Oʻz xalqi bilan yashaydi. Boshqa koʻz yoshi ham, oʻlim ham boʻlmaydi - abadiy doʻstlik.", "U yerda Khudo Awz khalqi bilan yashaydi. Boshqa kawz yoshi ham, awlim ham bawlmaydi - abadiy dawstlik.", "There God will dwell with his people. No more tears, no more death — fellowship forever.", "Revelation 21:3–4"],["Bu hikoya seniki ham boʻlishi mumkin. Isoga imon keltir, va uyingga qayt.", "Bu hikoya seniki ham bawlishi mumkin. Isoga imon keltir, va uyingga qayt.", "This story can be yours too. Believe in Jesus, and come home.", "John 3:16"]]}
  ]},
  {id:"fjesus",kind:'arc',title:"Jesus",ne:"Iso",
   overview:{t:"Who is Jesus?",ne:"Iso kim?",art:FUZ_ART.ovjesus,start:["Boshidan koʻraylik", "From here — his story in detail"],paras:[
    ["Muqaddas Kitobda Isoning koʻp ismlari bor - U Xudodir, insonlar orasida yashash uchun inson boʻlib kelgan.", "Muqaddas Kitobda Isoning kawp ismlari bor - U Khudodir, insonlar orasida yashash uchun inson bawlib kelgan.", "Jesus has many names in the Bible — he is God, who became flesh to dwell among human beings.", "John 1:1,14"],
    ["U biz yashagandek yashadi - ammo gunohsiz - va butun hayoti bizga Xudoning sevgisini koʻrsatdi.", "U biz yashagandek yashadi - ammo gunohsiz - va butun hayoti bizga Khudoning sevgisini kawrsatdi.", "He lived as we live — yet without sin — and his whole life showed us the love of God.", "Hebrews 4:15"],
    ["U biz uchun jonini berdi - gunohlarimiz bahosini toʻlash uchun xochda oʻldi. Va uchinchi kuni U oʻlimdan tirildi - oʻlimning oʻzini yengdi.", "U biz uchun jonini berdi - gunohlarimiz bahosini tawlash uchun khochda awldi. Va uchinchi kuni U awlimdan tirildi - awlimning awzini yengdi.", "He laid down his life for us — dying on a cross to pay the price of our sins. And on the third day he rose from the dead, defeating death itself.", "John 10:11 · 1 Corinthians 15:3–4"],
    ["Bugun Iso tirik, Xudoning oʻng tomonida oʻtiribdi. Va U hamon har bir insonni chaqiradi: ey charchaganlar va ogʻir yuk koʻtarganlar, hammangiz Mening oldimga kelinglar - Men sizga orom beraman.", "Bugun Iso tirik, Khudoning awng tomonida awtiribdi. Va U hamon har bir insonni chaqiradi: ey charchaganlar va oghir yuk kawtarganlar, hammangiz Mening oldimga kelinglar - Men sizga orom beraman.", "Today Jesus is alive, seated at the right hand of God. And he still calls every person: come to me, all you who are tired and carrying heavy loads, and I will give you rest.", "Hebrews 12:2 · Matthew 11:28"],
    ["Maqsad U haqida bilish emas - Uni tanishdir. Quyidagi hikoyalar shu taklifdir.", "Maqsad U haqida bilish emas - Uni tanishdir. Quyidagi hikoyalar shu taklifdir.", "The goal is not just to know about him — it is to know him. The stories below are that invitation.", "John 17:3"],
    ["Bundan keyin biz Uning hikoyasini boshidan - tugʻilishidan Uning oʻlimi va tirilishigacha, bir lahzadan keyin boshqasini - koʻrib chiqamiz.", "Bundan keyin biz Uning hikoyasini boshidan - tughilishidan Uning awlimi va tirilishigacha, bir lahzadan keyin boshqasini - kawrib chiqamiz.", "From here, we will walk through his story from the beginning — from his birth to his death and resurrection, one moment at a time."]]},
   sections:[
   {id:"jbirth",t:"The birth",ne:"Tugʻilish",art:FUZ_ART.jbirth,
    note:["Xudo saroylar, qoʻshinlar yoki boylik bilan kelmadi. Isoda Xudo kamtarlik bilan keldi - eng birinchi kechadanoq Oʻz xalqi orasida yashash va ularning hayotini boʻlishish uchun.", "Khudo saroylar, qawshinlar yoki boylik bilan kelmadi. Isoda Khudo kamtarlik bilan keldi - eng birinchi kechadanoq Awz khalqi orasida yashash va ularning hayotini bawlishish uchun.", "God did not arrive with palaces, armies or riches. In Jesus, God came humbly — to live among his people and share their life from the very first night."],
    paras:[["Iso tugʻilishidan yuzlab yillar oldin Isroil paygʻambarlari keladigan Zot haqida aytgan edilar - ular Uni kelajakdagi Masih deb bilardilar. Ular Unga koʻp nomlar berdilar - Ajoyib Maslahatchi, Qudratli Xudo, Abadiyat Otasi, Tinchlik Shahzodasi - va U bokira qizdan tugʻilishini yozdilar. Endi oʻsha bashorat amalga oshay deb turardi.", "Iso tughilishidan yuzlab yillar oldin Isroil payghambarlari keladigan Zot haqida aytgan edilar - ular Uni kelajakdagi Masih deb bilardilar. Ular Unga kawp nomlar berdilar - Ajoyib Maslahatchi, Qudratli Khudo, Abadiyat Otasi, Tinchlik Shahzodasi - va U bokira qizdan tughilishini yozdilar. Endi awsha bashorat amalga oshay deb turardi.", "Hundreds of years before Jesus was born, the prophets of Israel told of someone who would come — they knew him as the coming Messiah. They gave him many names — Wonderful Counselor, Mighty God, Everlasting Father, Prince of Peace — and they wrote that he would be born of a virgin. Now that prophecy was about to come true.", "Isaiah 9:6 · 7:14"],["Jabroil farishta Maryamga aytdi: sening oʻgʻling boʻladi, va Uning ismini Iso qoʻyasan.", "Jabroil farishta Maryamga aytdi: sening awghling bawladi, va Uning ismini Iso qawyasan.", "The angel Gabriel told Mary: you will have a son, and you are to name him Jesus.", "Luke 1:26–33"],["Maryam malika emas edi - Nosira qishlogʻidan chiqqan oddiy yosh ayol edi. Xudo Oʻzining eng buyuk ishlari uchun oddiy odamlarni tanlashni yaxshi koʻradi.", "Maryam malika emas edi - Nosira qishloghidan chiqqan oddiy yosh ayol edi. Khudo Awzining eng buyuk ishlari uchun oddiy odamlarni tanlashni yakhshi kawradi.", "Mary was no queen — just an ordinary young woman from the village of Nazareth. God loves to choose ordinary people for his greatest work.", "Luke 1:26–38"],["Vaqt kelganda Iso Baytlahmda tugʻildi - kichik bir shaharchada. Oila uchun qoladigan joy topilmadi, shuning uchun yangi tugʻilgan Iso oxurga - hayvonlarga yem soladigan idishga yotqizildi. Xudo dunyoga eng kamtarin joydan kirishni tanladi.", "Vaqt kelganda Iso Baytlahmda tughildi - kichik bir shaharchada. Oila uchun qoladigan joy topilmadi, shuning uchun yangi tughilgan Iso okhurga - hayvonlarga yem soladigan idishga yotqizildi. Khudo dunyoga eng kamtarin joydan kirishni tanladi.", "When the time came, Jesus was born in Bethlehem, a small town. There was no room for the family to stay, so the newborn Jesus was laid in a manger — a feeding box for animals. God chose to enter the world in the humblest of places.", "Luke 2:1–7"],["Uzoq sharqdan donishmandlar bir yulduz ortidan kelishdi. Ular bola oldida bosh egib, Unga qimmatbaho sovgʻalar taqdim etdilar.", "Uzoq sharqdan donishmandlar bir yulduz ortidan kelishdi. Ular bola oldida bosh egib, Unga qimmatbaho sovghalar taqdim etdilar.", "From the far east, wise men came following a star. They bowed before the child and offered him precious gifts.", "Matthew 2:1–11"],["Iso ismining oʻzi Uning vazifasini aytadi: U Oʻz xalqini gunohlaridan qutqaradi.", "Iso ismining awzi Uning vazifasini aytadi: U Awz khalqini gunohlaridan qutqaradi.", "The name Jesus means: he will save his people from their sins.", "Matthew 1:21"],["Oʻsha kecha farishtalar - Xudoning xabarchilari - yaqin dalalardagi choʻponlarga koʻrinib, xabarni eʼlon qildilar: eng yuksakda Xudoga shon-sharaf, va yer yuzida tinchlik! Vaʼda qilingan Qutqaruvchi tugʻilgan edi.", "Awsha kecha farishtalar - Khudoning khabarchilari - yaqin dalalardagi chawponlarga kawrinib, khabarni elon qildilar: eng yuksakda Khudoga shon-sharaf, va yer yuzida tinchlik! Vada qilingan Qutqaruvchi tughilgan edi.", "That night, angels — messengers from God — appeared to shepherds in the fields nearby, announcing the news: glory to God in the highest, and on earth peace! The promised Rescuer had been born.", "Luke 2:8–14"]]},
   {id:"jbaptism",t:"Baptism and the wilderness",ne:"Suvga choʻmdirilish va sahro",art:FUZ_ART.jbaptism,
    note:["Iso gunohkorlar bilan birga suvda turdi - va insonlar vasvasa oldida qayta-qayta yiqiladigan joyda Iso uni yengdi.", "Iso gunohkorlar bilan birga suvda turdi - va insonlar vasvasa oldida qayta-qayta yiqiladigan joyda Iso uni yengdi.", "Jesus stood in the water alongside sinners — and where human beings keep failing against temptation, Jesus overcame it."],
    paras:[["Yahyo ismli bir odam bor edi - Isroil xalqi uni paygʻambar deb bilardi. Iso daryo boʻyiga uning oldiga kelib, undan suvga choʻmdirildi. Iso suvdan chiqayotganda osmondan ovoz keldi: bu Mening sevikli Oʻgʻlim, Undan mamnunman.", "Yahyo ismli bir odam bor edi - Isroil khalqi uni payghambar deb bilardi. Iso daryo bawyiga uning oldiga kelib, undan suvga chawmdirildi. Iso suvdan chiqayotganda osmondan ovoz keldi: bu Mening sevikli Awghlim, Undan mamnunman.", "There was a man named John, whom the people of Israel regarded as a prophet. Jesus came to him at the river and was baptized by him. And as Jesus came up out of the water, a voice came from heaven: this is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased.", "Matthew 3:13–17"],["Soʻng Iso sahroga bordi, va u yerda shayton Uni sinadi - Uni Xudodan va Uning yoʻllaridan uzoqlashtirishga urindi. Ammo Iso gunoh qilmadi. U har bir vasvasada mustahkam turdi.", "Sawng Iso sahroga bordi, va u yerda shayton Uni sinadi - Uni Khudodan va Uning yawllaridan uzoqlashtirishga urindi. Ammo Iso gunoh qilmadi. U har bir vasvasada mustahkam turdi.", "Then Jesus went into the wilderness, and there the devil tempted him — trying to pull him away from God and his ways. But Jesus did not sin. He stood firm through every temptation.", "Matthew 4:1–11"],["Iso oddiy odamlarni Oʻziga shogird boʻlishga chaqira boshladi. Ularning koʻplari Uning ortidan ergashish va U bilan birga boʻlish uchun hamma narsani tashlab ketdilar.", "Iso oddiy odamlarni Awziga shogird bawlishga chaqira boshladi. Ularning kawplari Uning ortidan ergashish va U bilan birga bawlish uchun hamma narsani tashlab ketdilar.", "Jesus began calling ordinary people to be his disciples. Many of them left everything to follow him and to be with him.", "Mark 1:16–20"]]},
   {id:"jkingdom",t:"The kingdom announced",ne:"Shohlik eʼlon qilindi",art:FUZ_ART.jkingdom,
    note:["Xudoning Shohligi xaritadagi joy emas - bu Xudoning Oʻz yaxshi hukmronligi kirib kelayotgani, tuproqdan yorib chiqayotgan urugʻdek jimgina. Va uning eshigi eng kutilmagan odamlarga birinchi boʻlib ochiladi.", "Khudoning Shohligi kharitadagi joy emas - bu Khudoning Awz yakhshi hukmronligi kirib kelayotgani, tuproqdan yorib chiqayotgan urughdek jimgina. Va uning eshigi eng kutilmagan odamlarga birinchi bawlib ochiladi.", "The kingdom of God is not a place on a map — it is God’s own good rule breaking in, quiet as a seed pushing up through soil. And its door opens first to the least likely people."],
    paras:[["Iso eʼlon qildi: Xudoning Shohligi yaqinlashdi - Xudoning Oʻz yaxshi hukmronligi dunyoga kirib kelayotgan edi. Yashash yoʻlingizni oʻzgartiring, va Xushxabarga imon keltiring.", "Iso elon qildi: Khudoning Shohligi yaqinlashdi - Khudoning Awz yakhshi hukmronligi dunyoga kirib kelayotgan edi. Yashash yawlingizni awzgartiring, va Khushkhabarga imon keltiring.", "Jesus announced: the kingdom of God has come near — God’s own good rule was breaking into the world. Turn your way of living around, and believe the good news.", "Mark 1:15"],["U kambagʻallarni, kasallarni va gunohkorlarni Oʻziga yaqin chaqirdi - aynan boshqalar itarib yuborgan odamlarni. U uchun hech kim juda past yoki juda yoʻqolgan emas edi - Isoning yonida har biriga joy bor edi.", "U kambaghallarni, kasallarni va gunohkorlarni Awziga yaqin chaqirdi - aynan boshqalar itarib yuborgan odamlarni. U uchun hech kim juda past yoki juda yawqolgan emas edi - Isoning yonida har biriga joy bor edi.", "He called the poor, the sick and the sinners near — the very people others pushed away. Nobody was too low or too far gone for him; beside Jesus there was a place for each of them.", "Luke 5:27–32"],["Togʻ yonbagʻrida oʻtirib U oʻrgatdi: ruhan kambagʻallar baxtlidir, chunki osmon Shohligi ularnikidir. Kamtarlar baxtlidir. Tinchlik oʻrnatuvchilar baxtlidir. Dunyo mensimaydigan odamlarni Xudo baxtli deb ataydi.", "Togh yonbaghrida awtirib U awrgatdi: ruhan kambaghallar bakhtlidir, chunki osmon Shohligi ularnikidir. Kamtarlar bakhtlidir. Tinchlik awrnatuvchilar bakhtlidir. Dunyo mensimaydigan odamlarni Khudo bakhtli deb ataydi.", "Sitting on a hillside he taught: blessed are the poor in spirit, for the kingdom of heaven is theirs. Blessed are the humble. Blessed are the peacemakers. The very people the world looks down on, God calls blessed.", "Matthew 5:3–9"],["Odamlar kichik bolalarni Isoning oldiga olib kelishdi. Shogirdlari ularni qaytarmoqchi boʻldi - ammo Iso aytdi: bolalar Mening oldimga kelsin, ularni toʻsmanglar. Xudoning Shohligi shunaqalarnikidir.", "Odamlar kichik bolalarni Isoning oldiga olib kelishdi. Shogirdlari ularni qaytarmoqchi bawldi - ammo Iso aytdi: bolalar Mening oldimga kelsin, ularni tawsmanglar. Khudoning Shohligi shunaqalarnikidir.", "People brought little children to Jesus. His disciples turned them away — but Jesus said: let the children come to me, do not stop them. The kingdom of God belongs to such as these.", "Mark 10:13–14"],["Shohlik dalada yashiringan xazinaga oʻxshaydi: uni topgan odam quvonch bilan bor narsasini sotib, oʻsha dalani sotib oladi.", "Shohlik dalada yashiringan khazinaga awkhshaydi: uni topgan odam quvonch bilan bor narsasini sotib, awsha dalani sotib oladi.", "The kingdom is like treasure hidden in a field: the one who finds it joyfully sells everything to buy that field.", "Matthew 13:44"],["Iso aytdi: Xudoning Shohligi xantal urugʻiga oʻxshaydi - urugʻlarning eng kichigi, shunga qaramay oʻsib katta daraxt boʻladi, va qushlar uning shoxlarida uya quradi.", "Iso aytdi: Khudoning Shohligi khantal urughiga awkhshaydi - urughlarning eng kichigi, shunga qaramay awsib katta darakht bawladi, va qushlar uning shokhlarida uya quradi.", "Jesus said: the kingdom of God is like a mustard seed — the smallest of seeds, yet it grows into a great tree, and the birds nest in its branches.", "Mark 4:30–32"]]},
   {id:"jprayer",t:"Jesus teaches prayer",ne:"Iso ibodat oʻrgatadi",art:FUZ_ART.jprayer,
    note:["Xudo hamma narsaning Shohi boʻlsa ham, biz Uning oldiga dadil kela olamiz - bola otasining oldiga kelganidek. Iso ochgan eshik shudir.", "Khudo hamma narsaning Shohi bawlsa ham, biz Uning oldiga dadil kela olamiz - bola otasining oldiga kelganidek. Iso ochgan eshik shudir.", "Even though God is the King of everything, we can come to him confidently — the way a child comes to a father. That is the door Jesus opened."],
    paras:[["Iso erta tongda yolgʻiz ibodat qilish uchun chiqib ketardi. Izdoshlari soʻradilar: Rabbiy, bizga ham ibodat qilishni oʻrgat.", "Iso erta tongda yolghiz ibodat qilish uchun chiqib ketardi. Izdoshlari sawradilar: Rabbiy, bizga ham ibodat qilishni awrgat.", "Jesus would go out early in the morning to pray alone. His followers asked: Lord, teach us to pray too.", "Mark 1:35 · Luke 11:1"],["U ularga oʻrgatdi: shunday ibodat qilinglar - osmondagi Otamiz, Sening isming muqaddas sanalsin, Sening Shohliging kelsin.", "U ularga awrgatdi: shunday ibodat qilinglar - osmondagi Otamiz, Sening isming muqaddas sanalsin, Sening Shohliging kelsin.", "He taught them: pray like this — our Father in heaven, may your name be honored as holy, may your kingdom come.", "Matthew 6:9–10"],["Bugungi kerakli nonimizni bizga ber. Gunohlarimizni kechir, biz ham bizga yomonlik qilganlarni kechirganimiz kabi.", "Bugungi kerakli nonimizni bizga ber. Gunohlarimizni kechir, biz ham bizga yomonlik qilganlarni kechirganimiz kabi.", "Give us today the food we need. Forgive our sins, as we also forgive those who wrong us.", "Matthew 6:11–12"],["Va bizni vasvasaga solma, balki yovuzlikdan qutqar. Bugun ham butun dunyo boʻylab Isoning izdoshlari shu ibodatni oʻqiydilar.", "Va bizni vasvasaga solma, balki yovuzlikdan qutqar. Bugun ham butun dunyo bawylab Isoning izdoshlari shu ibodatni awqiydilar.", "And lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from evil. Followers of Jesus around the world still pray this prayer today.", "Matthew 6:13"],["Ibodat uzun nutq emas - bu Otang bilan suhbatlashishdir. Va Xudo eshitadi.", "Ibodat uzun nutq emas - bu Otang bilan suhbatlashishdir. Va Khudo eshitadi.", "Prayer is not a long speech — it is talking with your Father. And God listens.", "Matthew 6:7–8"],["Iso aytdi: soʻranglar, va sizga beriladi. Qidiringlar, va topasizlar. Taqillatinglar, va eshik ochiladi.", "Iso aytdi: sawranglar, va sizga beriladi. Qidiringlar, va topasizlar. Taqillatinglar, va eshik ochiladi.", "Jesus said: ask, and it will be given to you. Seek, and you will find. Knock, and the door will be opened.", "Matthew 7:7"]]},
   {id:"jmiracles",t:"Power and compassion",ne:"Qudrat va rahm",art:FUZ_ART.jmiracles,
    note:["Moʻjizalar sehr emas - ular oldindan koʻrsatishdir. Har bir shifo, har bir tinchlangan boʻron, har bir koʻpaygan non Xudo istagan dunyoga ochilgan derazadir.", "Mawjizalar sehr emas - ular oldindan kawrsatishdir. Har bir shifo, har bir tinchlangan bawron, har bir kawpaygan non Khudo istagan dunyoga ochilgan derazadir.", "The miracles are not magic — they are previews. Every healing, every calmed storm, every multiplied loaf is a window into the world as God intends it."],
    paras:[["Iso kasallarga shifo berdi va koʻrlarga koʻz ochdi.", "Iso kasallarga shifo berdi va kawrlarga kawz ochdi.", "Jesus healed the sick and gave the blind their sight.", "Matthew 9"],["Isoning oldiga moxov kasalligi bilan bir odam keldi - hech kim tegmaydigan odam. Iso qoʻlini uzatdi, unga tegdi va aytdi: pok boʻl.", "Isoning oldiga mokhov kasalligi bilan bir odam keldi - hech kim tegmaydigan odam. Iso qawlini uzatdi, unga tegdi va aytdi: pok bawl.", "A man with leprosy came to Jesus — a man nobody would touch. Jesus reached out his hand, touched him, and said: be healed.", "Mark 1:40–42"],["U bitta soʻz bilan boʻronni tinchlantirdi. Shogirdlari bir-biridan soʻrashdi: bu axir kim?", "U bitta sawz bilan bawronni tinchlantirdi. Shogirdlari bir-biridan sawrashdi: bu akhir kim?", "He calmed a storm with a word. His disciples asked each other: who IS this?", "Mark 4:35–41"],["Beshta non va ikkita baliq bilan U minglab odamni toʻydirdi.", "Beshta non va ikkita baliq bilan U minglab odamni tawydirdi.", "With five loaves and two fish he fed thousands.", "John 6:1–14"],["Oʻlgan kichkina qizning qoʻlidan ushlab U aytdi: bolam, tur. Va qiz turdi. Hatto oʻlim ham Uning soʻziga boʻysunadi.", "Awlgan kichkina qizning qawlidan ushlab U aytdi: bolam, tur. Va qiz turdi. Hatto awlim ham Uning sawziga bawysunadi.", "Taking the hand of a little girl who had died, he said: child, get up. And she rose. Even death obeys his word.", "Mark 5:41–42"],["U oddiy odamlar bilan yurdi - baliqchilar, gunohkor deb atalganlar, singanlar va kasallar - va ularni sogʻaytirdi. U bizga singan odamlar uchun Xudoning sevgisi va mehri qanchalik chuqurligini koʻrsatdi.", "U oddiy odamlar bilan yurdi - baliqchilar, gunohkor deb atalganlar, singanlar va kasallar - va ularni soghaytirdi. U bizga singan odamlar uchun Khudoning sevgisi va mehri qanchalik chuqurligini kawrsatdi.", "He walked with ordinary people — fishermen, so-called sinners, the broken and the sick — and he made them well. He showed us how deep the love and kindness of God is for us as broken people.", "Matthew 9:35–36"]]},
   {id:"jlostson",t:"The lost son",ne:"Yoʻqolgan oʻgʻil",art:FUZ_ART.jlostson,
    
    paras:[["Dindor odamlar Iso haqida norozilik bildirardilar: bu odam gunohkorlarni qabul qiladi - hatto ular bilan birga ovqatlanadi! Javoban Iso bu hikoyani aytdi. Bir oʻgʻil otasining mol-mulkini olib, uzoq yurtga ketdi va hammasini sovurdi.", "Dindor odamlar Iso haqida norozilik bildirardilar: bu odam gunohkorlarni qabul qiladi - hatto ular bilan birga ovqatlanadi! Javoban Iso bu hikoyani aytdi. Bir awghil otasining mol-mulkini olib, uzoq yurtga ketdi va hammasini sovurdi.", "The religious people grumbled about Jesus: this man welcomes sinners — he even eats with them! In answer, Jesus told this story. A son took his father’s wealth, went far away, and wasted it all.", "Luke 15:1–2 · 11–16"],["Uzoq yurtda oʻgʻil shu qadar ochqadiki, choʻchqalarning yemini yeyishga tayyor boʻldi. Shunda u oʻziga keldi: otamning xizmatkorlari ham toʻyib ovqatlanadi. Men uyga qaytaman.", "Uzoq yurtda awghil shu qadar ochqadiki, chawchqalarning yemini yeyishga tayyor bawldi. Shunda u awziga keldi: otamning khizmatkorlari ham tawyib ovqatlanadi. Men uyga qaytaman.", "In the far country the son grew so hungry he was ready to eat the pigs’ food. Then he came to his senses: even my father’s servants eat their fill. I will go home.", "Luke 15:14–19"],["Oʻgʻil uyga kelganda, ota unga tomon YUGURDI va uni quchoqlab oldi.", "Awghil uyga kelganda, ota unga tomon YUGURDI va uni quchoqlab oldi.", "When the son came home, the father RAN to him and threw his arms around him.", "Luke 15:20–24"],["Xudoning yuragi shundaydir: uyiga qaytgan har bir kishini U quvonch bilan qabul qiladi.", "Khudoning yuragi shundaydir: uyiga qaytgan har bir kishini U quvonch bilan qabul qiladi.", "That is the heart of God: he joyfully welcomes everyone who comes home.", "Luke 15"],["Ammo katta oʻgʻil gʻazablandi: shuncha yil men senga xizmat qildim! Ota aytdi: oʻgʻlim, menda bor narsaning hammasi seniki. Ammo uking yoʻqolgan edi va topildi - qanday qilib quvonmasak boʻladi? Baʼzida Xudoning shunchalik rahmdilligi bizga malol keladi - ammo bu Uni eng singan odamni ham kechirishdan va sevishdan toʻxtatmaydi.", "Ammo katta awghil ghazablandi: shuncha yil men senga khizmat qildim! Ota aytdi: awghlim, menda bor narsaning hammasi seniki. Ammo uking yawqolgan edi va topildi - qanday qilib quvonmasak bawladi? Bazida Khudoning shunchalik rahmdilligi bizga malol keladi - ammo bu Uni eng singan odamni ham kechirishdan va sevishdan tawkhtatmaydi.", "But the elder son was angry: all these years I have served you! The father said: son, everything I have is yours. But your brother was lost and is found — how could we not celebrate? Sometimes we are offended at how merciful God is — but that does not stop him from forgiving and loving even the most broken.", "Luke 15:25–32"]]},
   {id:"jsamaritan",t:"The good Samaritan",ne:"Yaxshi samariyalik",art:FUZ_ART.jsamaritan,
    note:["Iso bizni dunyo dushmanlarimiz deb aytadigan odamlarni ham - bizdan farq qiladigan odamlarni ham sevishga chaqiradi.", "Iso bizni dunyo dushmanlarimiz deb aytadigan odamlarni ham - bizdan farq qiladigan odamlarni ham sevishga chaqiradi.", "Jesus calls us to love even the people the world tells us are our enemies — people who are different from us."],
    paras:[["Iso odamlarga Xudoni sevishni va qoʻshnisini sevishni oʻrgatdi. Kimdir Undan soʻradi: lekin mening qoʻshnim kim? U hikoya bilan javob berdi.", "Iso odamlarga Khudoni sevishni va qawshnisini sevishni awrgatdi. Kimdir Undan sawradi: lekin mening qawshnim kim? U hikoya bilan javob berdi.", "Jesus taught people to love God and to love their neighbor. Someone asked him: but who is my neighbor? He answered with a story.", "Luke 10:25–29"],["Bir yahudiy odam ikki shahar orasidagi kimsasiz yoʻlda - Quddusdan Yerixoga tushib ketayotgan edi. Qaroqchilar unga hujum qildilar: uni urdilar, bor narsasini tortib oldilar va yoʻl chetida yarim oʻlik holda tashlab ketdilar.", "Bir yahudiy odam ikki shahar orasidagi kimsasiz yawlda - Quddusdan Yerikhoga tushib ketayotgan edi. Qaroqchilar unga hujum qildilar: uni urdilar, bor narsasini tortib oldilar va yawl chetida yarim awlik holda tashlab ketdilar.", "A Jewish man was traveling the lonely road between two cities — from Jerusalem down to Jericho. Robbers attacked him: they beat him, took everything he had, and left him half dead beside the road.", "Luke 10:30"],["Diniy rahbarlar yarador odamning yonidan oʻtib ketdilar. Ammo bir samariyalik - begona odam - toʻxtadi va unga gʻamxoʻrlik qildi.", "Diniy rahbarlar yarador odamning yonidan awtib ketdilar. Ammo bir samariyalik - begona odam - tawkhtadi va unga ghamkhawrlik qildi.", "Religious leaders passed the wounded man by. But a Samaritan — an outsider — stopped and cared for him.", "Luke 10:30–35"],
["Hikoyani hayratlanarli qilgan narsa shu: oʻsha kunlarda yahudiylar va samariyaliklar bir-birini yomon koʻrardilar. Yarador yahudiy odam uchun samariyalik dushman degani edi - ammo toʻxtagan aynan oʻsha dushman boʻldi.", "Hikoyani hayratlanarli qilgan narsa shu: awsha kunlarda yahudiylar va samariyaliklar bir-birini yomon kawrardilar. Yarador yahudiy odam uchun samariyalik dushman degani edi - ammo tawkhtagan aynan awsha dushman bawldi.", "Here is what made the story shocking: in those days Jews and Samaritans despised each other. To the wounded Jewish man, a Samaritan meant an enemy — yet the enemy was the one who stopped.", "John 4:9"],["U yaralarga moy va sharob quydi, odamni oʻz uloviga mindirdi, mehmonxonaga olib keldi - va pul toʻlab vaʼda berdi: bundan ortiq nima sarflansa, men qaytaraman.", "U yaralarga moy va sharob quydi, odamni awz uloviga mindirdi, mehmonkhonaga olib keldi - va pul tawlab vada berdi: bundan ortiq nima sarflansa, men qaytaraman.", "He poured oil and wine on the wounds, set the man on his own donkey, brought him to an inn — and paid, promising: whatever more it costs, I will repay.", "Luke 10:34–35"],["Iso aytdi: bor, va sen ham shunday qil.", "Iso aytdi: bor, va sen ham shunday qil.", "Jesus said: go and do the same.", "Luke 10:37"]]},
   {id:"jbuilders",t:"The two builders",ne:"Ikki quruvchi",art:FUZ_ART.jbuilders,
    note:["Iso buyuk vaʼzini savol bilan tugatdi: hayoting nima ustiga qurilgan? Uning soʻzlarini eshitish yaxshi - ammo ular boʻyicha chindan yashaydigan odam qoya ustiga quradi, va boʻron kelganda oʻsha uy turib qoladi.", "Iso buyuk vazini savol bilan tugatdi: hayoting nima ustiga qurilgan? Uning sawzlarini eshitish yakhshi - ammo ular bawyicha chindan yashaydigan odam qoya ustiga quradi, va bawron kelganda awsha uy turib qoladi.", "Jesus ended his great sermon with a question: what is your life built on? Hearing his words is good — but the person who actually lives them is building on rock, and that house stands when the storm comes."],
    paras:[["Iso aytdi: kim Mening soʻzlarimni eshitib, ularni bajarsa, u uyini qoya ustiga qurgan dono odamga oʻxshaydi.", "Iso aytdi: kim Mening sawzlarimni eshitib, ularni bajarsa, u uyini qoya ustiga qurgan dono odamga awkhshaydi.", "Jesus said: whoever hears my words and does them is like a wise man who built his house on the rock.", "Matthew 7:24"],["Yomgʻir yogʻdi, suv toshdi, shamol urdi - ammo oʻsha uy qulamadi, chunki uning poydevori qoya ustida edi.", "Yomghir yoghdi, suv toshdi, shamol urdi - ammo awsha uy qulamadi, chunki uning poydevori qoya ustida edi.", "The rain came, the floods rose, the winds blew — but that house did not fall, because its foundation was on the rock.", "Matthew 7:25"],["Ammo eshitib ham bajarmaydigan odam qum ustiga qurgan nodonga oʻxshaydi - boʻron kelganda, oʻsha uy katta shovqin bilan quladi.", "Ammo eshitib ham bajarmaydigan odam qum ustiga qurgan nodonga awkhshaydi - bawron kelganda, awsha uy katta shovqin bilan quladi.", "But the one who hears and does not act is like a fool who built on sand — when the storm came, that house fell with a great crash.", "Matthew 7:26–27"],["Tashqaridan ikkala uy bir xil koʻrinardi. Farq faqat boʻron kelganda koʻrindi. Poydevorlar sinov bilan ochiladi.", "Tashqaridan ikkala uy bir khil kawrinardi. Farq faqat bawron kelganda kawrindi. Poydevorlar sinov bilan ochiladi.", "From the outside the two houses looked the same. The difference showed only when the storm came. Foundations are revealed by testing.", "Matthew 7:24–27"]]},
   {id:"jcross",t:"The cross",ne:"Xoch",art:FUZ_ART.jcross,
    note:["Xoch Isoning vazifasini toʻxtatgan tasodif emas edi - u vazifaning OʻZI edi. Hech kim Uning jonini olmadi; U oʻzi berdi, va sevgi toʻliq narxni ixtiyoriy toʻladi.", "Khoch Isoning vazifasini tawkhtatgan tasodif emas edi - u vazifaning AWZI edi. Hech kim Uning jonini olmadi; U awzi berdi, va sevgi tawliq narkhni ikhtiyoriy tawladi.", "The cross was not an accident that interrupted Jesus’ mission — it WAS the mission. Nobody took his life; he laid it down, love paying the full price willingly."],
    paras:[["Doʻstlaring uchun joningni berishdan katta sevgi yoʻq - va Iso aynan shuni qildi.", "Dawstlaring uchun joningni berishdan katta sevgi yawq - va Iso aynan shuni qildi.", "There is no greater love than to lay down your life for your friends — and that is exactly what Jesus did.", "John 15:13"],["Diniy rahbarlarning hasadi Uni oʻlimga olib bordi. Ammo Iso allaqachon aytgan edi: hech kim jonimni Mendan olmaydi - Men uni Oʻzim beraman.", "Diniy rahbarlarning hasadi Uni awlimga olib bordi. Ammo Iso allaqachon aytgan edi: hech kim jonimni Mendan olmaydi - Men uni Awzim beraman.", "The envy of the religious leaders drove him to his death. But Jesus had already said: no one takes my life from me — I lay it down myself.", "Matthew 27:18 · John 10:18"],["Uni xochga mixlayotganlarida ham Iso Oʻzini oʻldirayotgan oʻsha odamlar uchun ibodat qildi: Ota, ularni kechir, chunki ular nima qilayotganlarini bilmaydilar.", "Uni khochga mikhlayotganlarida ham Iso Awzini awldirayotgan awsha odamlar uchun ibodat qildi: Ota, ularni kechir, chunki ular nima qilayotganlarini bilmaydilar.", "Even as they nailed him to the cross, Jesus prayed for the very people who were killing him: Father, forgive them, for they do not know what they are doing.", "Luke 23:34"],["Yuzlab yillar oldin paygʻambarlar yozgan edilar: kelajak Xudoning Xizmatkori bizning aybimiz uchun yaralanadi va gunohimizni Oʻzi koʻtaradi. Xochda oʻsha bashorat amalga oshdi: Iso hammamizning gunohimizni koʻtarayotgan edi.", "Yuzlab yillar oldin payghambarlar yozgan edilar: kelajak Khudoning Khizmatkori bizning aybimiz uchun yaralanadi va gunohimizni Awzi kawtaradi. Khochda awsha bashorat amalga oshdi: Iso hammamizning gunohimizni kawtarayotgan edi.", "Hundreds of years earlier, the prophets had written that the coming Servant of God would be wounded for our wrongdoing and would carry our sin himself. On the cross that prophecy came true: Jesus was carrying the sin of us all.", "Isaiah 53:5–6 · 1 Peter 2:24"],["U Otaning sevgisi va Shohligini ochish uchun kelgan edi - shunga qaramay biz Uni rad etdik; insonlar Uni oʻldirdilar. Ammo na biz, na biz boʻysungan qorongʻu kuchlar bu boshidanoq rejaning bir qismi ekanini bilmasdik. Isoning oʻlimi orqali Xudoning Shohligi osmonda boʻlgani kabi yer yuzida ham kelayotgan edi.", "U Otaning sevgisi va Shohligini ochish uchun kelgan edi - shunga qaramay biz Uni rad etdik; insonlar Uni awldirdilar. Ammo na biz, na biz bawysungan qoronghu kuchlar bu boshidanoq rejaning bir qismi ekanini bilmasdik. Isoning awlimi orqali Khudoning Shohligi osmonda bawlgani kabi yer yuzida ham kelayotgan edi.", "He had come to reveal the Father’s love and kingdom — yet we rejected him; human beings killed him. But neither we nor the dark forces we obeyed knew this was part of the plan all along. Through Jesus’ death, God’s kingdom was coming on earth as it is in heaven.", "Acts 2:23 · 1 Corinthians 2:8"],["Isoning yonida ikki jinoyatchi osilgan edi. Biri aytdi: Iso, Shohligingga kirganingda meni esla. Iso javob berdi: bugun sen Men bilan jannatda boʻlasan.", "Isoning yonida ikki jinoyatchi osilgan edi. Biri aytdi: Iso, Shohligingga kirganingda meni esla. Iso javob berdi: bugun sen Men bilan jannatda bawlasan.", "Two criminals hung beside Jesus. One said: Jesus, remember me when you come into your kingdom. Jesus answered: today you will be with me in paradise.", "Luke 23:39–43"],["U aytdi: tamom boʻldi. Gunohimizning narxi toʻliq toʻlandi.", "U aytdi: tamom bawldi. Gunohimizning narkhi tawliq tawlandi.", "He said: it is finished. The price of our sin was fully paid.", "John 19:30"]]},
   {id:"jrisen",t:"He is risen",ne:"U tirildi",art:FUZ_ART.jrisen,
    note:["Hammasi shu tongga suyanadi - Iso tirilgani uchun gunoh bahosi toʻlangan, oʻlim yengilgan, va Xudoga qaytish yoʻli ochiq.", "Hammasi shu tongga suyanadi - Iso tirilgani uchun gunoh bahosi tawlangan, awlim yengilgan, va Khudoga qaytish yawli ochiq.", "Everything stands on this morning: because Jesus rose, the price of sin is paid, death is defeated, and the way back to God stands open."],
    paras:[["Iso qabrga qoʻyildi - ogʻir tosh bilan yopilgan dafn gʻoriga. Ammo yakshanba tongi erta, Uning ortidan yurgan ayollar qabrga kelganlarida, tosh dumalatib qoʻyilgan va qabr boʻsh edi. Iso oʻlimdan tirilgan edi.", "Iso qabrga qawyildi - oghir tosh bilan yopilgan dafn ghoriga. Ammo yakshanba tongi erta, Uning ortidan yurgan ayollar qabrga kelganlarida, tosh dumalatib qawyilgan va qabr bawsh edi. Iso awlimdan tirilgan edi.", "Jesus was buried in a tomb — a burial cave closed with a heavy stone. But early on Sunday morning, when women who followed him came to the tomb, the stone was rolled away and the tomb was empty. Jesus had risen from the dead.", "Luke 24:1–8"],["Ulardan biri, Magdalalik Maryam, qabr tashqarisida yigʻlab turardi - kimdir Uning jasadini olib ketgan deb oʻylardi. Shunda Isoning Oʻzi uning qarshisida turdi. Koʻz yoshlari orasidan u Uni tanimadi, toki U uning ismini aytmaguncha: Maryam. Oʻsha lahzada u tanidi - oʻlimini koʻrgan ustozi tirik, va U uni ismidan biladi.", "Ulardan biri, Magdalalik Maryam, qabr tashqarisida yighlab turardi - kimdir Uning jasadini olib ketgan deb awylardi. Shunda Isoning Awzi uning qarshisida turdi. Kawz yoshlari orasidan u Uni tanimadi, toki U uning ismini aytmaguncha: Maryam. Awsha lahzada u tanidi - awlimini kawrgan ustozi tirik, va U uni ismidan biladi.", "One of them, Mary Magdalene, stood outside the tomb weeping — she thought someone had taken his body away. Then Jesus himself stood before her. Through her tears she did not recognize him, until he said her name: Mary. In that moment she knew — the teacher she had watched die was alive, and he knew her by name.", "John 20:11–16"],["Isoning shogirdlaridan biri, Toʻmas ismli, Iso oʻlimdan tirilganiga ishona olmadi. U aytdi: Uning qoʻllaridagi mix izlarini koʻrmagunimcha ishonmayman. Soʻng Iso kelib, ularning orasida turdi va Toʻmasga aytdi: qoʻllarimga qara - tegib koʻr. Toʻmas baqirdi: Rabbim va Xudoyim!", "Isoning shogirdlaridan biri, Tawmas ismli, Iso awlimdan tirilganiga ishona olmadi. U aytdi: Uning qawllaridagi mikh izlarini kawrmagunimcha ishonmayman. Sawng Iso kelib, ularning orasida turdi va Tawmasga aytdi: qawllarimga qara - tegib kawr. Tawmas baqirdi: Rabbim va Khudoyim!", "One of Jesus’ disciples, named Thomas, could not believe that Jesus had risen from the dead. He said: unless I see the nail marks in his hands, I will not believe. Then Jesus came, stood among them, and said to Thomas: look at my hands — touch and see. Thomas cried out: my Lord and my God!", "John 20:24–29"],["Isoning oʻlimi va tirilishi orqali insonlar Xudo bilan yarashtirildi. U gunohlarimiz jazosini toʻladi, va insoniyatni changalida tutib turgan qorongʻu kuchlarni yengdi.", "Isoning awlimi va tirilishi orqali insonlar Khudo bilan yarashtirildi. U gunohlarimiz jazosini tawladi, va insoniyatni changalida tutib turgan qoronghu kuchlarni yengdi.", "Through Jesus’ death and resurrection, human beings were reconciled to God. He paid the penalty for our sins, and he defeated the dark powers that held humanity in their grip.", "Romans 5:10 · Colossians 2:15"],["Soʻng tirilgan Iso shogirdlariga topshiriq berdi: boringlar, barcha xalqlarni shogird qilinglar - va esda tutinglar, Men har kuni siz bilanman.", "Sawng tirilgan Iso shogirdlariga topshiriq berdi: boringlar, barcha khalqlarni shogird qilinglar - va esda tutinglar, Men har kuni siz bilanman.", "The risen Jesus then commissioned his disciples: go and make disciples of all nations — and remember, I am with you always.", "Matthew 28:18–20"],["Soʻng, ularning koʻz oʻngida, Iso osmonga koʻtarildi. U ularga shaharda qolib, Otaning vaʼdasini kutishni buyurgan edi - ular bilan yashash uchun keladigan Muqaddas Ruhni. Va Uning izdoshlari hikoyasi aynan oʻsha yerdan boshlanadi.", "Sawng, ularning kawz awngida, Iso osmonga kawtarildi. U ularga shaharda qolib, Otaning vadasini kutishni buyurgan edi - ular bilan yashash uchun keladigan Muqaddas Ruhni. Va Uning izdoshlari hikoyasi aynan awsha yerdan boshlanadi.", "Then, before their eyes, Jesus was taken up into heaven. He had told them to wait in the city for the promise of the Father — the Holy Spirit, who would come to dwell with them. And that is where the story of his followers begins.", "Luke 24:49–51 · Acts 1:4–9"]]}
  ]},

{id:'facts',kind:'arc',title:'Jesus’ Followers',ne:'Isoning shogirdlari',
sections:[
{id:'await',t:'Wait for the gift',ne:'Inʼomni kutish',art:FUZ_ART.await,

paras:[
['Tirilganidan keyin qirq kun davomida Iso doʻstlari bilan uchrashib turdi — ular bilan ovqatlanib, Xudoning Shohligi haqida oʻrgatib. U chindan ham tirik edi.','Tirilganidan keyin qirq kun davomida Iso dawstlari bilan uchrashib turdi — ular bilan ovqatlanib, Khudoning Shohligi haqida awrgatib. U chindan ham tirik edi.','For forty days after he rose, Jesus kept meeting his friends — eating with them, teaching them about God’s kingdom. He was unmistakably alive.','Acts 1:3'],
['U bitta vaʼda va bitta vazifa berdi — Muqaddas Ruh ustingizga tushguncha Quddusda kutinglar; keyin sizlar Mening guvohlarim boʻlasizlar — bu shaharda, qoʻshni yurtda va yerning eng chekkasigacha.','U bitta vada va bitta vazifa berdi — Muqaddas Ruh ustingizga tushguncha Quddusda kutinglar; keyin sizlar Mening guvohlarim bawlasizlar — bu shaharda, qawshni yurtda va yerning eng chekkasigacha.','He gave them a promise and a task: wait in Jerusalem until the Holy Spirit comes upon you — then you will be my witnesses, in this city, in the next country, and to the very ends of the earth.','Acts 1:4–8'],
["Keyin, ular qarab turganda, U yuqoriga koʻtarildi va bulut Uni koʻzlardan yashirdi. Ikki farishta yonlarida turib ularga dedi — mana shu Iso qaytib keladi, xuddi ketganini koʻrganingizdek.", "Keyin, ular qarab turganda, U yuqoriga kawtarildi va bulut Uni kawzlardan yashirdi. Ikki farishta yonlarida turib ularga dedi — mana shu Iso qaytib keladi, khuddi ketganini kawrganingizdek.", "Then, as they watched, he was taken up, and a cloud hid him from their eyes. Two angels stood beside them and told them: this same Jesus will come back, the same way you saw him go.", "Acts 1:9–11"],
["Shunday qilib, bir yuz yigirmaga yaqin kishi yuqori xonada birga kutishdi — erkagu ayollar — va ular ibodat qilishdi.", "Shunday qilib, bir yuz yigirmaga yaqin kishi yuqori khonada birga kutishdi — erkagu ayollar — va ular ibodat qilishdi.", "So about a hundred and twenty of them waited together in an upstairs room — men and women — and they prayed.", "Acts 1:12–14"]]},
{id:'pentecost',t:'Wind and fire',ne:'Shamol va olov',art:FUZ_ART.pentecost,

paras:[
["Shogirdlar yuqori xonada birga boʻlgan paytda, hosil bayrami — Pentikost deb ataladigan bayram uchun Quddus odamga toʻla edi — har yurtdan kelgan mehmonlar bilan.", "Shogirdlar yuqori khonada birga bawlgan paytda, hosil bayrami — Pentikost deb ataladigan bayram uchun Quddus odamga tawla edi — har yurtdan kelgan mehmonlar bilan.", "While the disciples were together in the upstairs room, Jerusalem was crowded for the harvest festival called Pentecost, with visitors from every land.", "Acts 2:1,5"],
['Toʻsatdan kuchli shamol shovqiniday tovush uyni toʻldirdi va olovning kichik tillariga oʻxshagan narsalar har birining ustiga qoʻndi. Hammalari Muqaddas Ruhga toʻlishdi.','Tawsatdan kuchli shamol shovqiniday tovush uyni tawldirdi va olovning kichik tillariga awkhshagan narsalar har birining ustiga qawndi. Hammalari Muqaddas Ruhga tawlishdi.','Suddenly a sound like a rushing wind filled the house, and what looked like small flames of fire rested on each of them. All of them were filled with the Holy Spirit.','Acts 2:2–4'],
['Ular hech qachon oʻrganmagan tillarda gapira boshlashdi — mehmonlar esa, har biri oʻz ona tilida, Xudoning buyuk ishlari haqida eshitdi.','Ular hech qachon awrganmagan tillarda gapira boshlashdi — mehmonlar esa, har biri awz ona tilida, Khudoning buyuk ishlari haqida eshitdi.','They began to speak in languages they had never learned — and the visitors heard, each in their own mother tongue, the great things God has done.','Acts 2:4–11'],
['Xudo odamlar bilan ularning oʻz tilida gaplashishni yaxshi koʻradi — yurak tili, ona tili. Bugun ham shunday qiladi.','Khudo odamlar bilan ularning awz tilida gaplashishni yakhshi kawradi — yurak tili, ona tili. Bugun ham shunday qiladi.','God loves to speak to people in their own language — heart-language, mother tongue. He still does.'],
["Keyin Butrus — bir paytlar Isodan tongan oʻsha baliqchi — Quddusdagi katta olomon oldida oʻrnidan turib, butun hikoyani aytib berdi: sizlar Uni oʻldirdingizlar; Xudo Uni tiriltirdi; U — Rabbiy. Tinglovchilarning yuragi ezildi — endi nima qilaylik?", "Keyin Butrus — bir paytlar Isodan tongan awsha baliqchi — Quddusdagi katta olomon oldida awrnidan turib, butun hikoyani aytib berdi: sizlar Uni awldirdingizlar; Khudo Uni tiriltirdi; U — Rabbiy. Tinglovchilarning yuragi ezildi — endi nima qilaylik?", "Then Peter — the fisherman who had once denied Jesus — stood up in front of a large crowd of people in Jerusalem and told the whole story: you killed him; God raised him; he is Lord. The listeners were cut to the heart: what should we do?", "Acts 2:14–37"],
["Xudoga qaytinglar va suvga choʻmdirilinglar, dedi Butrus, shunda sizlar ham xuddi shu inʼomni olasizlar. Oʻsha kuni uch mingga yaqin odam imon keltirdi.", "Khudoga qaytinglar va suvga chawmdirilinglar, dedi Butrus, shunda sizlar ham khuddi shu inomni olasizlar. Awsha kuni uch mingga yaqin odam imon keltirdi.", "Turn back to God and be baptized, Peter said, and you will receive the same gift. That day about three thousand people believed.", "Acts 2:38–41"]]},
{id:'together',t:'Life together',ne:'Birgalikdagi hayot',art:FUZ_ART.together,

paras:[
['Yangi imonlilar toʻrt narsaga berilib ketishdi: havoriylarning taʼlimi, birodarlik, birga non sindirish va ibodat.','Yangi imonlilar tawrt narsaga berilib ketishdi: havoriylarning talimi, birodarlik, birga non sindirish va ibodat.','The new believers devoted themselves to four things: the apostles’ teaching, fellowship, breaking bread together, and prayer.','Acts 2:42'],
['Ular quvonch bilan bir-birining uyida ovqatlanishardi. Hech kim muhtoj boʻlmasligi uchun ortiqcha narsalarini sotib boʻlishishardi.','Ular quvonch bilan bir-birining uyida ovqatlanishardi. Hech kim muhtoj bawlmasligi uchun ortiqcha narsalarini sotib bawlishishardi.','They ate in each other’s homes with glad hearts. They sold what they could spare so that no one among them was in need.','Acts 2:44–46'],
['Boy va kambagʻal, erkak va ayol, mahalliy va musofir — hammasi bitta dasturxon atrofida oʻtirdi. Qon boʻyicha emas, Iso boʻyicha oila.','Boy va kambaghal, erkak va ayol, mahalliy va musofir — hammasi bitta dasturkhon atrofida awtirdi. Qon bawyicha emas, Iso bawyicha oila.','Rich and poor, men and women, locals and foreigners sat at one table — a family not of blood, but of Jesus.'],
["Ana shu birgalikdagi hayot jamoat deb ataladi. Jamoat hech qachon bino boʻlmagan — jamoat Isoniki boʻlgan odamlardir.", "Ana shu birgalikdagi hayot jamoat deb ataladi. Jamoat hech qachon bino bawlmagan — jamoat Isoniki bawlgan odamlardir.", "This life together is called the church. The church was never a building; it is people who belong to Jesus."],
['Va kundan-kunga qoʻshnilar kuzatib turishdi — kundan-kunga Xudo ularning soniga yana odamlar qoʻshib bordi.','Va kundan-kunga qawshnilar kuzatib turishdi — kundan-kunga Khudo ularning soniga yana odamlar qawshib bordi.','And day by day their neighbors watched — and day by day, God added more people to their number.','Acts 2:47']]},
{id:'boldness',t:'In the name of Jesus',ne:'Isoning nomi bilan',art:FUZ_ART.boldness,

paras:[
["Quddusdagi maʼbad darvozasida tugʻilishidan yura olmaydigan bir tilanchi oʻtirardi — uni har kuni oʻsha yerga olib kelishardi, shuning uchun hamma uni tanirdi. Bir kuni Butrus bilan Yuhanno ibodatga ketayotib uning yonidan oʻtishdi, va u ulardan pul soʻradi.", "Quddusdagi mabad darvozasida tughilishidan yura olmaydigan bir tilanchi awtirardi — uni har kuni awsha yerga olib kelishardi, shuning uchun hamma uni tanirdi. Bir kuni Butrus bilan Yuhanno ibodatga ketayotib uning yonidan awtishdi, va u ulardan pul sawradi.", "At the temple gate in Jerusalem sat a beggar who had been lame from birth — everyone knew him, for he was carried there every day. One day Peter and John walked past him on their way to pray, and he asked them for money.", "Acts 3:1–3"],
['Kumushim ham, oltinim ham yoʻq, dedi Butrus, lekin borimni senga beraman — nosiralik Iso Masihning nomi bilan oʻrningdan tur va yur. U esa yurdi — yurib, sakrab, Xudoni olqishlab.','Kumushim ham, oltinim ham yawq, dedi Butrus, lekin borimni senga beraman — nosiralik Iso Masihning nomi bilan awrningdan tur va yur. U esa yurdi — yurib, sakrab, Khudoni olqishlab.','Silver and gold I do not have, Peter said, but what I have I give you: in the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth, stand up and walk. And he did — walking, and leaping, and praising God.','Acts 3:6–8'],
['Diniy rahbarlar ularni qamab, buyruq berishdi — bu nomni boshqa hech qachon tilga olmanglar.','Diniy rahbarlar ularni qamab, buyruq berishdi — bu nomni boshqa hech qachon tilga olmanglar.','The religious authorities arrested them and ordered them: never speak this name again.','Acts 4:1–3,18'],
['Butrus bilan Yuhanno javob berishdi — Xudodan koʻra sizlarga quloq solish toʻgʻrimi, oʻzlaringiz hukm qilinglar — biz koʻrgan va eshitganlarimizni aytmasdan turolmaymiz.','Butrus bilan Yuhanno javob berishdi — Khudodan kawra sizlarga quloq solish tawghrimi, awzlaringiz hukm qilinglar — biz kawrgan va eshitganlarimizni aytmasdan turolmaymiz.','Peter and John answered: judge for yourselves whether it is right to obey you rather than God — we cannot stop speaking about what we have seen and heard.','Acts 4:19–20'],
["Kengash hayron qoldi — bular oddiy, oʻqimagan odamlar edi — va ular bu odamlar Iso bilan birga boʻlganini tanib olishdi.", "Kengash hayron qoldi — bular oddiy, awqimagan odamlar edi — va ular bu odamlar Iso bilan birga bawlganini tanib olishdi.", "The council was astonished: these were ordinary, unschooled men — and they recognized that these men had been with Jesus.", "Acts 4:13"]]},
{id:'scattered',t:'Scattered seed',ne:'Sochilgan urugʻ',art:FUZ_ART.scattered,

paras:[
["Hamma ham xabarni yaxshi kutib olmadi. Stefan ismli bir imonli — inoyat va qudratga toʻla odam — diniy rahbarlar kengashi oldiga sudrab keltirildi.", "Hamma ham khabarni yakhshi kutib olmadi. Stefan ismli bir imonli — inoyat va qudratga tawla odam — diniy rahbarlar kengashi oldiga sudrab keltirildi.", "Not everyone welcomed the message. A believer named Stephen — full of grace and power — was dragged before a council of religious leaders.", "Acts 6:8–12"],
["U Xudo xalqining butun hikoyasini aytib berdi va oxirida dedi — sizlar oʻsha Solihga xiyonat qilib, Uni oʻldirdingizlar. Chunki Isoni oʻlimga topshirganlar aynan shu diniy rahbarlar edi.", "U Khudo khalqining butun hikoyasini aytib berdi va okhirida dedi — sizlar awsha Solihga khiyonat qilib, Uni awldirdingizlar. Chunki Isoni awlimga topshirganlar aynan shu diniy rahbarlar edi.", "He told them the whole story of God’s people, and then he said: you have betrayed and murdered the Righteous One. For it was these same religious leaders who had handed Jesus over to be put to death.", "Acts 7:51–52"],
['Ular uni toshboʻron qilishdi. Jon berayotib u oʻz Rabbiysi kabi ibodat qildi — Rabbiy, bu gunohni ularning hisobiga qoʻyma. U Iso uchun jon bergan birinchi odam boʻldi.','Ular uni toshbawron qilishdi. Jon berayotib u awz Rabbiysi kabi ibodat qildi — Rabbiy, bu gunohni ularning hisobiga qawyma. U Iso uchun jon bergan birinchi odam bawldi.','They stoned him. As he died he prayed like his Lord: Lord, do not hold this sin against them. He was the first to die for Jesus.','Acts 7:59–60'],
['Oʻsha kundan boshlab katta quvgʻin boshlandi va imonlilar Quddusdan tarqalib ketishdi. Hammasi tugaganday koʻrindi.','Awsha kundan boshlab katta quvghin boshlandi va imonlilar Quddusdan tarqalib ketishdi. Hammasi tugaganday kawrindi.','A great persecution broke out that day, and the believers were scattered from Jerusalem. It looked like the end.','Acts 8:1'],
["Lekin qayerga tarqalishsa, xabarni ham oʻsha yerga olib borishdi — shahar ketidan shaharda yangi jamoatlar unib chiqdi.", "Lekin qayerga tarqalishsa, khabarni ham awsha yerga olib borishdi — shahar ketidan shaharda yangi jamoatlar unib chiqdi.", "But wherever they were scattered, they carried the message with them — and new churches sprang up in town after town.", "Acts 8:4"]]},
{id:'damascus',t:'The enemy becomes a brother',ne:'Dushman birodarga aylanadi',art:FUZ_ART.damascus,
note:["Isoning qoʻli yetmaydigan odam yoʻq — hatto jamoatning eng yomon dushmani ham.", "Isoning qawli yetmaydigan odam yawq — hatto jamoatning eng yomon dushmani ham.", "Nobody is beyond the reach of Jesus — not even the church’s worst enemy."],
paras:[
['Jamoatning eng shafqatsiz ovchisi Shoul ismli bir yigit edi. U uyma-uy yurib, imonlilarni zindonga sudrardi — Stefanning oʻldirilishiga ham rozi boʻlgan edi.','Jamoatning eng shafqatsiz ovchisi Shoul ismli bir yigit edi. U uyma-uy yurib, imonlilarni zindonga sudrardi — Stefanning awldirilishiga ham rozi bawlgan edi.','The fiercest hunter of the church was a young man named Saul. He went house to house, dragging believers to prison — and he approved of Stephen’s death.','Acts 8:1,3'],
["Bir kuni Shoul u yerdagi imonlilarni qoʻlga olish uchun Damashq shahriga ketayotgan edi — yoʻlda toʻsatdan osmondan bir nur uning atrofida chaqnadi va u yerga yiqildi. Bir ovoz keldi — Shoul, Shoul, nega Meni quvgʻin qilyapsan?", "Bir kuni Shoul u yerdagi imonlilarni qawlga olish uchun Damashq shahriga ketayotgan edi — yawlda tawsatdan osmondan bir nur uning atrofida chaqnadi va u yerga yiqildi. Bir ovoz keldi — Shoul, Shoul, nega Meni quvghin qilyapsan?", "One day, as Saul was traveling to the city of Damascus to arrest the believers there, a light from heaven suddenly flashed around him, and he fell to the ground. A voice said: Saul, Saul, why do you persecute me?", "Acts 9:3–4"],
['Rabbiy, Sen kimsan? — deb soʻradi u. Men sen quvgʻin qilayotgan Isoman.','Rabbiy, Sen kimsan? — deb sawradi u. Men sen quvghin qilayotgan Isoman.','Who are you, Lord? he asked. I am Jesus, whom you are persecuting.','Acts 9:5'],
['Eʼtibor bering — Iso Mening odamlarimni demadi — Meni dedi. Uning odamlariga tekkan narsa Unga tegadi.','Etibor bering — Iso Mening odamlarimni demadi — Meni dedi. Uning odamlariga tekkan narsa Unga tegadi.','Notice: Jesus did not say “my people” — he said ME. Whatever touches his people touches him.'],
["Yerdan turganida Shoul koʻra olmasdi — Iso bilan boʻlgan oʻsha uchrashuv uni koʻr qilib qoʻygan edi. Hamrohlari uni yetaklab shaharga olib kirishdi, u uch kun koʻr boʻlib qoldi — hech narsa yemadi, hech narsa ichmadi.", "Yerdan turganida Shoul kawra olmasdi — Iso bilan bawlgan awsha uchrashuv uni kawr qilib qawygan edi. Hamrohlari uni yetaklab shaharga olib kirishdi, u uch kun kawr bawlib qoldi — hech narsa yemadi, hech narsa ichmadi.", "When Saul got up from the ground, he could not see — his meeting with Jesus had left him blind. His companions led him by the hand into the city, and for three days he stayed blind, and he neither ate nor drank.", "Acts 9:8–9"],
["Damashqda Ananiya ismli bir imonli yashardi. Iso vahiyda unga dedi — Shoulning oldiga bor. Ananiya qoʻrqdi — bu odam imonlilarga qancha yomonlik qilganini bilardi — lekin u itoat qildi. U qoʻllarini Shoulning ustiga qoʻyib dedi — birodarim Shoul, yana koʻrishing va Muqaddas Ruhga toʻlishing uchun Iso meni yubordi. Shu zahoti Shoul yana koʻra boshladi, oʻrnidan turib suvga choʻmdirildi.", "Damashqda Ananiya ismli bir imonli yashardi. Iso vahiyda unga dedi — Shoulning oldiga bor. Ananiya qawrqdi — bu odam imonlilarga qancha yomonlik qilganini bilardi — lekin u itoat qildi. U qawllarini Shoulning ustiga qawyib dedi — birodarim Shoul, yana kawrishing va Muqaddas Ruhga tawlishing uchun Iso meni yubordi. Shu zahoti Shoul yana kawra boshladi, awrnidan turib suvga chawmdirildi.", "In Damascus there lived a believer named Ananias. Jesus told him in a vision: go to Saul. Ananias was afraid — he knew how much harm this man had done to the believers — but he obeyed. He laid his hands on Saul and said: Brother Saul, Jesus has sent me so that you may see again and be filled with the Holy Spirit. At once Saul could see again, and he got up and was baptized.", "Acts 9:10–18"],
['Ovchi elchiga aylandi. Bugun biz uni Pavlus deb bilamiz — Xushxabarni hammadan uzoqqa olib boradigan odam.','Ovchi elchiga aylandi. Bugun biz uni Pavlus deb bilamiz — Khushkhabarni hammadan uzoqqa olib boradigan odam.','The hunter became a messenger. We know him today as Paul — who would carry the good news further than anyone.','Acts 9:20–22']]},
{id:'cornelius',t:'No outsiders anymore',ne:'Endi begona yoʻq',art:FUZ_ART.cornelius,
note:['Endi begona qolmadi. Hech bir xalq, hech bir urugʻ, hech bir tabaqa Xudoga boshqasidan yaqinroq emas — eshik hammaga barobar ochiq, barobar yaqin.','Endi begona qolmadi. Hech bir khalq, hech bir urugh, hech bir tabaqa Khudoga boshqasidan yaqinroq emas — eshik hammaga barobar ochiq, barobar yaqin.','There are no outsiders left. No nation, no clan, no caste stands closer to God than another — the door is equally open, and equally near.'],
paras:[
["Oʻsha paytlarda koʻpchilik Xushxabar faqat Isroilniki deb oʻylardi — Isoga ergashmoqchi boʻlgan har kim avval yahudiy boʻlishi kerak deb. Xudo eshikni keng ochmoqchi edi.", "Awsha paytlarda kawpchilik Khushkhabar faqat Isroilniki deb awylardi — Isoga ergashmoqchi bawlgan har kim avval yahudiy bawlishi kerak deb. Khudo eshikni keng ochmoqchi edi.", "In those days many believed the good news belonged only to Israel — that anyone who wanted to follow Jesus must first become a Jew. God was about to open the door wide."],
["Korniliy ismli bir rimlik harbiy bor edi — musofir, lekin Xudodan qoʻrqadigan va Unga ibodat qiladigan odam. Bir kuni u vahiyda Xudoning farishtasini koʻrdi, farishta unga dedi — Yaffa shahriga odam yubor va Butrus ismli kishini chaqirtir.", "Korniliy ismli bir rimlik harbiy bor edi — musofir, lekin Khudodan qawrqadigan va Unga ibodat qiladigan odam. Bir kuni u vahiyda Khudoning farishtasini kawrdi, farishta unga dedi — Yaffa shahriga odam yubor va Butrus ismli kishini chaqirtir.", "There was a Roman army officer named Cornelius — a foreigner, yet a man who feared God and prayed to him. One day he saw an angel of God in a vision, and the angel told him: send men to the city of Joppa, and bring back a man named Peter.", "Acts 10:1–5"],
["Ayni paytda Butrus ham vahiy koʻrdi — osmondan katta bir dasturxon tushdi, har xil hayvonlarga toʻla — jumladan uning xalqiga yeyish taqiqlangan hayvonlar ham. Bir ovoz keldi — tur, Butrus, soʻyib ye. Butrus rad etganda ovoz javob berdi — Xudo pok qilgan narsani harom dema. Bu uch marta yuz berdi.", "Ayni paytda Butrus ham vahiy kawrdi — osmondan katta bir dasturkhon tushdi, har khil hayvonlarga tawla — jumladan uning khalqiga yeyish taqiqlangan hayvonlar ham. Bir ovoz keldi — tur, Butrus, sawyib ye. Butrus rad etganda ovoz javob berdi — Khudo pok qilgan narsani harom dema. Bu uch marta yuz berdi.", "Meanwhile Peter also saw a vision: a great sheet came down from heaven, filled with every kind of animal — including animals his people were forbidden to eat. A voice said: get up, Peter, kill and eat. When Peter refused, the voice answered: do not call unclean what God has made clean. This happened three times.", "Acts 10:9–16"],
["Xuddi shu payt Korniliyning odamlari eshikni taqillatishdi, va Butrus vahiyning maʼnosini tushundi — gap taom haqida emas, odamlar haqida edi — Xudoning nazarida hech bir inson harom emas. Odatga koʻra musofirning uyiga kirish unga taqiqlangan edi, lekin Butrus u odamlar bilan bordi — va ichkariga kirdi.", "Khuddi shu payt Korniliyning odamlari eshikni taqillatishdi, va Butrus vahiyning manosini tushundi — gap taom haqida emas, odamlar haqida edi — Khudoning nazarida hech bir inson harom emas. Odatga kawra musofirning uyiga kirish unga taqiqlangan edi, lekin Butrus u odamlar bilan bordi — va ichkariga kirdi.", "Just then the messengers from Cornelius knocked at the door, and Peter understood what the vision meant: it was not about food but about people — no person is unclean in God’s eyes. By custom it was forbidden for him to enter a foreigner’s house, but Peter went with the messengers, and he went in.", "Acts 10:17–29"],
['Butrus hali Iso haqida gapirayotganda Muqaddas Ruh tinglayotganlarning hammasiga tushdi — oʻsha musofirlarga ham, boshida ularga tushganidek.','Butrus hali Iso haqida gapirayotganda Muqaddas Ruh tinglayotganlarning hammasiga tushdi — awsha musofirlarga ham, boshida ularga tushganidek.','While Peter was still speaking about Jesus, the Holy Spirit fell on everyone listening — on the foreigners, exactly as on them at the beginning.','Acts 10:44–47'],
['Butrus dedi — endi chinakam tushundim: Xudo tarafkashlik qilmaydi, balki Unga yuz burgan har bir xalqning odamlarini qabul qiladi.','Butrus dedi — endi chinakam tushundim: Khudo tarafkashlik qilmaydi, balki Unga yuz burgan har bir khalqning odamlarini qabul qiladi.','Peter said: now I truly understand — God shows no favoritism, but welcomes people from every nation who turn to him.','Acts 10:34–35']]},
{id:'sent',t:'Sent out',ne:'Yuborilganlar',art:FUZ_ART.sent,

paras:[
['Antioxiya shahrida — imonlilar birinchi marta masihiylar deb atalgan joyda — jamoat ibodat va roʻza tutish bilan band edi.','Antiokhiya shahrida — imonlilar birinchi marta masihiylar deb atalgan joyda — jamoat ibodat va rawza tutish bilan band edi.','In the city of Antioch — where believers were first called Christians — the church was praying and fasting.','Acts 11:26 · 13:1–2'],
['Muqaddas Ruh dedi — Barnabo bilan Shoulni Men chaqirgan ish uchun ajratinglar. Jamoat ularga qoʻl qoʻyib, yoʻlga kuzatib qoʻydi.','Muqaddas Ruh dedi — Barnabo bilan Shoulni Men chaqirgan ish uchun ajratinglar. Jamoat ularga qawl qawyib, yawlga kuzatib qawydi.','The Holy Spirit said: set apart for me Barnabas and Saul, for the work I have called them to. The church laid hands on them and sent them off.','Acts 13:2–3'],
['Shunday qilib safarlar boshlandi — shahar ketidan shaharda ular Isoning hikoyasini aytib, ortlarida imonlilarning yangi oilalarini qoldirishdi.','Shunday qilib safarlar boshlandi — shahar ketidan shaharda ular Isoning hikoyasini aytib, ortlarida imonlilarning yangi oilalarini qoldirishdi.','So began the journeys: city after city, they told the story of Jesus, and left behind new families of believers.','Acts 13–14'],
['Har yoʻlda mashaqqat bor edi — masxara, toshboʻron, zindon. Pavlus keyinroq yozdi — Xudoning Shohligiga kirish uchun biz koʻp azob-uqubatlardan oʻtishimiz kerak.','Har yawlda mashaqqat bor edi — maskhara, toshbawron, zindon. Pavlus keyinroq yozdi — Khudoning Shohligiga kirish uchun biz kawp azob-uqubatlardan awtishimiz kerak.','There was hardship on every road — mockery, stoning, prison. Paul later wrote: we must go through many troubles to enter God’s kingdom.','Acts 14:19–22'],
["Yosh jamoatlarga yaqin boʻlish uchun Pavlus ularga maktublar yozdi. Oʻsha maktublarning koʻpini biz bugun ham oʻqiymiz — ular Yangi Ahdda.", "Yosh jamoatlarga yaqin bawlish uchun Pavlus ularga maktublar yozdi. Awsha maktublarning kawpini biz bugun ham awqiymiz — ular Yangi Ahdda.", "To stay close to the young churches, Paul wrote them letters. We still read many of these letters today — they are in the New Testament."]]},
{id:'chains',t:'Chains cannot stop it',ne:'Zanjirlar toʻxtatolmaydi',art:FUZ_ART.chains,
note:["Insoniyatni qutqarish boʻlgan Xudoning maqsadini hech qanday quvgʻin toʻxtata olmaydi — zanjirlar elchilarni bogʻlay olardi, lekin xabarni hech qachon bogʻlay olmadi.", "Insoniyatni qutqarish bawlgan Khudoning maqsadini hech qanday quvghin tawkhtata olmaydi — zanjirlar elchilarni boghlay olardi, lekin khabarni hech qachon boghlay olmadi.", "God’s purpose to save humanity cannot be stopped by any amount of persecution — chains could hold the messengers, but never the message."],
paras:[
["Filippi shahrida Pavlus va uning doʻsti Silas odamlarga Iso haqida gapirayotganda ushlanib, tayoq bilan urildi. Keyin ularni zindonning eng ichki xonasiga qamashdi va oyoqlarini yogʻoch kishanga solishdi.", "Filippi shahrida Pavlus va uning dawsti Silas odamlarga Iso haqida gapirayotganda ushlanib, tayoq bilan urildi. Keyin ularni zindonning eng ichki khonasiga qamashdi va oyoqlarini yoghoch kishanga solishdi.", "In the city of Philippi, Paul and his friend Silas were telling people about Jesus when they were seized and beaten with rods. Then they were thrown into the innermost cell of the prison, and their feet were locked in wooden stocks.", "Acts 16:22–24"],
['Yarim tunda ular ibodat qilib, Xudoga qoʻshiq aytishardi — boshqa mahbuslar esa tinglab turishardi.','Yarim tunda ular ibodat qilib, Khudoga qawshiq aytishardi — boshqa mahbuslar esa tinglab turishardi.','At midnight they were praying and singing to God — and the other prisoners were listening.','Acts 16:25'],
['Toʻsatdan zilzila zindonni larzaga keltirdi; hamma eshiklar ochilib ketdi, hamma zanjirlar yechilib tushdi.','Tawsatdan zilzila zindonni larzaga keltirdi; hamma eshiklar ochilib ketdi, hamma zanjirlar yechilib tushdi.','Suddenly an earthquake shook the prison; every door flew open, every chain came loose.','Acts 16:26'],
["Zindonboshi uygʻonib, zindon eshiklari ochiq turganini koʻrdi. Mahbuslar qochib ketgan deb oʻylab, oʻzini oʻldirish uchun qilichini sugʻurdi — lekin Pavlus qichqirdi — oʻzingga zarar yetkazma, hammamiz shu yerdamiz! Zindonboshi titrab ularning oldiga yiqildi va qichqirdi — najot topishim uchun nima qilay? Ular javob berishdi — Rabbiy Isoga imon keltir, shunda najot topasan — sen ham, oilang ham. Oʻsha kechasiyoq u ularning yaralarini yuvdi, oʻzi va butun oilasi suvga choʻmdirildi.", "Zindonboshi uyghonib, zindon eshiklari ochiq turganini kawrdi. Mahbuslar qochib ketgan deb awylab, awzini awldirish uchun qilichini sughurdi — lekin Pavlus qichqirdi — awzingga zarar yetkazma, hammamiz shu yerdamiz! Zindonboshi titrab ularning oldiga yiqildi va qichqirdi — najot topishim uchun nima qilay? Ular javob berishdi — Rabbiy Isoga imon keltir, shunda najot topasan — sen ham, oilang ham. Awsha kechasiyoq u ularning yaralarini yuvdi, awzi va butun oilasi suvga chawmdirildi.", "The jailer woke and saw the prison doors open. Sure that the prisoners had escaped, he drew his sword to take his own life — but Paul called out: do not harm yourself, we are all here! Trembling, the jailer fell down before them and cried: what must I do to be saved? They answered: believe in the Lord Jesus, and you will be saved — you and your household. That very night he washed their wounds, and he and his whole family were baptized.", "Acts 16:27–34"]]},
{id:'ends',t:'To the ends of the earth',ne:'Yerning chekkalarigacha',art:FUZ_ART.ends,

paras:[
['Sizlar Mening guvohlarim boʻlasizlar, degan edi Iso — yerning eng chekkasigacha. Ular boʻlishdi ham — ular aytgan odamlar ham, ulardan keyingilar ham.','Sizlar Mening guvohlarim bawlasizlar, degan edi Iso — yerning eng chekkasigacha. Ular bawlishdi ham — ular aytgan odamlar ham, ulardan keyingilar ham.','You will be my witnesses, Jesus had said — to the very ends of the earth. And they were — and so were the ones they told, and the ones after them.','Acts 1:8'],
["Xabar sahrolar, togʻlar va dengizlardan oʻtdi va tildan tilga tarjima qilindi.", "Khabar sahrolar, toghlar va dengizlardan awtdi va tildan tilga tarjima qilindi.", "The message crossed deserts and mountains and oceans, and it was translated into language after language."],
['Asrdan asrga oddiy guvohlar uni olgʻa olib borishdi — savdogarlar, onalar, oʻqituvchilar, dehqonlar — bir kuni u Oʻzbekistonga ham yetib kelguncha.','Asrdan asrga oddiy guvohlar uni olgha olib borishdi — savdogarlar, onalar, awqituvchilar, dehqonlar — bir kuni u Awzbekistonga ham yetib kelguncha.','Century after century, ordinary witnesses carried it on — traders, mothers, teachers, farmers — until one day it reached Uzbekistan too.'],
['Bugun Oʻzbekistonda Isoning shogirdlari yigʻilishadi, ibodat qilishadi va qoʻshnilarini yaxshi koʻrishadi — oʻsha yuqori xonada boshlangan oilaning bir qismi.','Bugun Awzbekistonda Isoning shogirdlari yighilishadi, ibodat qilishadi va qawshnilarini yakhshi kawrishadi — awsha yuqori khonada boshlangan oilaning bir qismi.','Today, followers of Jesus in Uzbekistan gather, pray and love their neighbors — part of the same family that began in that upstairs room.'],
["Bibliyaning oxirgi kitobida — Vahiy deb ataladigan kitobda — Isoning shogirdlaridan biri, Yuhanno ismli kishiga hikoyaning oxiri koʻrsatildi — sanab boʻlmas olomon, har bir xalqdan, urugʻdan, eldan va tildan, Xudoning huzurida birga turibdi. Oʻsha suratda sening xalqingdan ham kimdir bor.", "Bibliyaning okhirgi kitobida — Vahiy deb ataladigan kitobda — Isoning shogirdlaridan biri, Yuhanno ismli kishiga hikoyaning okhiri kawrsatildi — sanab bawlmas olomon, har bir khalqdan, urughdan, eldan va tildan, Khudoning huzurida birga turibdi. Awsha suratda sening khalqingdan ham kimdir bor.", "In the last book of the Bible, called Revelation, one of Jesus’ disciples — a man named John — was shown the end of the story: a crowd no one could count, from every nation, tribe, people and language, standing together before God. Someone from your people is in that picture.", "Revelation 7:9"],
["Havoriylar kitobida Xudo nima qilgan boʻlsa, bugun ham xalqlar orasida xuddi shuni qilmoqda — guvohlarini yubormoqda, adashgan va singanlarni qutqarmoqda.", "Havoriylar kitobida Khudo nima qilgan bawlsa, bugun ham khalqlar orasida khuddi shuni qilmoqda — guvohlarini yubormoqda, adashgan va singanlarni qutqarmoqda.", "God is still doing among the nations today what he was doing in the book of Acts — sending his witnesses, and saving the lost and the broken."]]}
]},

{id:"ffollow",kind:"arc",title:"Following Jesus Yourself",ne:"Isoga oʻzing ergashish",
sections:[
{id:"community",t:"Christian community",ne:"Masihiy jamiyat",art:FUZ_ART.community,
note:["Isoga ergashish hech qachon yolgʻiz qilinadigan ish boʻlmagan. Birinchi kundanoq Uning izdoshlari birga yurishgan.", "Isoga ergashish hech qachon yolghiz qilinadigan ish bawlmagan. Birinchi kundanoq Uning izdoshlari birga yurishgan.", "Following Jesus was never meant to be done alone. From the very first day, his followers have walked together."],
paras:[
["Agar Isoga ergashmoqchi boʻlsang, qoʻyishing mumkin boʻlgan eng yaxshi qadamlardan biri — Unga ergashadigan boshqa odamlarni topish. Masihiy jamiyat, koʻpincha jamoat deb ataladi.", "Agar Isoga ergashmoqchi bawlsang, qawyishing mumkin bawlgan eng yakhshi qadamlardan biri — Unga ergashadigan boshqa odamlarni topish. Masihiy jamiyat, kawpincha jamoat deb ataladi.", "If you want to follow Jesus, one of the best steps you can take is to find other people who follow him — a Christian community, often called a church."],
["Jamoat bino emas; odamlardir. Isoni sevadigan, Bibliyani oʻqiydigan va seni kutib oladigan guruhni izla — u katta zalda, kichkina xonada yoki birovning uyida yigʻilishi mumkin.", "Jamoat bino emas; odamlardir. Isoni sevadigan, Bibliyani awqiydigan va seni kutib oladigan guruhni izla — u katta zalda, kichkina khonada yoki birovning uyida yighilishi mumkin.", "A church is not a building; it is people. Look for a group that loves Jesus, reads the Bible, and welcomes you — it may meet in a big hall, a small room, or someone’s home."],
["Birinchi imonlilar doim birga yigʻilishardi: ular birga sajda qilishar, oʻrganishar, ovqatlanishar va ibodat qilishar, qiyin kunlarda bir-biriga yordam berishardi. Sogʻlom masihiy jamiyat bugun ham xuddi shunday koʻrinadi.", "Birinchi imonlilar doim birga yighilishardi: ular birga sajda qilishar, awrganishar, ovqatlanishar va ibodat qilishar, qiyin kunlarda bir-biriga yordam berishardi. Soghlom masihiy jamiyat bugun ham khuddi shunday kawrinadi.", "The first believers met together constantly: they worshiped, learned, ate and prayed together, and helped each other through hard times. That is still what a healthy Christian community looks like.", "Acts 2:42–47"],
["Bibliya imonlilarni birga yigʻilishni tashlamaslikka, balki bir-birini ruhlantirishda davom etishga undaydi — chunki birga boʻlsak kuchli qolamiz.", "Bibliya imonlilarni birga yighilishni tashlamaslikka, balki bir-birini ruhlantirishda davom etishga undaydi — chunki birga bawlsak kuchli qolamiz.", "The Bible urges believers not to give up meeting together, but to keep encouraging one another — because together we stay strong.", "Hebrews 10:24–25"],
["Xudodan seni shunday jamiyatga yetaklashini soʻra. Baʼzi joylarda u kichkina, hatto yashirin boʻladi — lekin Iso vaʼda bergan: ikki yoki uch kishi Mening nomimda yigʻilgan joyda Men ularning orasidaman.", "Khudodan seni shunday jamiyatga yetaklashini sawra. Bazi joylarda u kichkina, hatto yashirin bawladi — lekin Iso vada bergan: ikki yoki uch kishi Mening nomimda yighilgan joyda Men ularning orasidaman.", "Ask God to lead you to such a community. In some places it is small, or even hidden — but Jesus promised: where two or three gather in my name, I am there among them.", "Matthew 18:20"]]},
{id:"bible",t:"Bible study",ne:"Bibliyani oʻrganish",art:FUZ_ART.bible,
note:["Bhasaly-da oʻqigan hamma narsang — Bibliyadan olingan, qayta aytilgan va tushuntirilgan boʻlaklar. Toʻliq hikoya u yerda seni kutmoqda.", "Bhasaly-da awqigan hamma narsang — Bibliyadan olingan, qayta aytilgan va tushuntirilgan bawlaklar. Tawliq hikoya u yerda seni kutmoqda.", "Everything you have read on Bhasaly is pieces of the Bible, taken out, retold and explained. The full story is waiting for you there."],
paras:[
["Xudo Bibliya orqali gapiradi — va sen uni oʻzing oʻqiy olasan. More sahifasidan oʻz tilingdagi Bibliyani telefoningga yuklab olishing yoki kitob doʻkonidan sotib olishing mumkin.", "Khudo Bibliya orqali gapiradi — va sen uni awzing awqiy olasan. More sahifasidan awz tilingdagi Bibliyani telefoningga yuklab olishing yoki kitob dawkonidan sotib olishing mumkin.", "God speaks through the Bible — and you can read it yourself. You can download the Bible on your phone in your own language from the More page, or buy one from a book store."],
["Bibliya bitta kitob emas, butun bir kutubxona — koʻp asrlar davomida yozilgan, lekin yagona hikoyani aytadi: Xudoning insoniyat bilan hikoyasi, Isoga olib boradigan hikoya.", "Bibliya bitta kitob emas, butun bir kutubkhona — kawp asrlar davomida yozilgan, lekin yagona hikoyani aytadi: Khudoning insoniyat bilan hikoyasi, Isoga olib boradigan hikoya.", "The Bible is not one book but a whole library — written down over many centuries, telling one single story: God’s story with humanity, which leads to Jesus.", "2 Timothy 3:16"],
["Oʻqishni boshlash uchun yaxshi joy — Luqo kitobi: guvohlarning soʻzlaridan sinchiklab tuzilgan Isoning hayoti. Keyin Havoriylarni oʻqi — Uning izdoshlari hikoyasi — va Yangi Ahdning qolgan qismini davom ettir.", "Awqishni boshlash uchun yakhshi joy — Luqo kitobi: guvohlarning sawzlaridan sinchiklab tuzilgan Isoning hayoti. Keyin Havoriylarni awqi — Uning izdoshlari hikoyasi — va Yangi Ahdning qolgan qismini davom ettir.", "A good place to start reading is the book of Luke — the life of Jesus, carefully put together from eyewitness accounts. Then read Acts, the story of his followers — and continue through the rest of the New Testament.", "Luke 1:1–4"],
["Undan keyin Eski Ahdni oʻqish ham foydali — eng boshidan Xudo va insoniyat tarixi, Iso uchun yoʻl tayyorlaydigan tarix.", "Undan keyin Eski Ahdni awqish ham foydali — eng boshidan Khudo va insoniyat tarikhi, Iso uchun yawl tayyorlaydigan tarikh.", "After that, it also helps to read the Old Testament — the history of God and humanity from the very beginning, which prepares the way for Jesus."],
["Har kuni ozgina oʻqi, oʻqishdan oldin esa tushunishga yordam berishini Xudodan soʻra. More sahifasidagi Bibliya ilovasida Bibliya boʻylab qadam-baqadam yetaklaydigan oʻqish rejalari ham bor.", "Har kuni ozgina awqi, awqishdan oldin esa tushunishga yordam berishini Khudodan sawra. More sahifasidagi Bibliya ilovasida Bibliya bawylab qadam-baqadam yetaklaydigan awqish rejalari ham bor.", "Read a little every day, and before you read, ask God to help you understand. The Bible app on the More page also offers guided reading plans that walk you through the Bible step by step."]]},
{id:"prayer",t:"Prayer and worship",ne:"Ibodat va sajda",art:FUZ_ART.prayer,
note:["Ibodat mutaxassislar uchun marosim emas. Bu — tinglashni yaxshi koʻradigan ota bilan bolaning suhbati.", "Ibodat mutakhasislar uchun marosim emas. Bu — tinglashni yakhshi kawradigan ota bilan bolaning suhbati.", "Prayer is not a ritual for experts. It is a child talking with a father who loves to listen."],
paras:[
["Ibodat — bu shunchaki Xudo bilan gaplashish — oʻz soʻzlaring bilan, oʻz tilingda. Maxsus soʻzlar ham, maxsus joy ham kerak emas; Xudo seni hamma joyda, har qanday paytda eshitadi.", "Ibodat — bu shunchaki Khudo bilan gaplashish — awz sawzlaring bilan, awz tilingda. Makhsus sawzlar ham, makhsus joy ham kerak emas; Khudo seni hamma joyda, har qanday paytda eshitadi.", "Prayer is simply talking with God — in your own words, in your own language. You do not need special words or a special place; God hears you anywhere, at any time.", "Matthew 6:7–8"],
["Ibodat uchun foydali bir namunada toʻrt qadam bor — inglizchada bu toʻrttasi ACTS soʻzini hosil qiladi: hamdu sano, gunohni tan olish, shukr, iltijo.", "Ibodat uchun foydali bir namunada tawrt qadam bor — inglizchada bu tawrttasi ACTS sawzini hosil qiladi: hamdu sano, gunohni tan olish, shukr, iltijo.", "One helpful pattern for prayer has four steps — in English they spell the word ACTS: Adoration, Confession, Thanksgiving, Supplication."],
["Hamdu sano — Xudoni U kimligi uchun ulugʻlash demak. Gunohni tan olish — gunohlaringni Unga halol tan olish demak — U allaqachon biladi va kechirishga sodiqdir.", "Hamdu sano — Khudoni U kimligi uchun ulughlash demak. Gunohni tan olish — gunohlaringni Unga halol tan olish demak — U allaqachon biladi va kechirishga sodiqdir.", "Adoration means praising God for who he is. Confession means honestly admitting your sins to him — he already knows, and he is faithful to forgive.", "1 John 1:9"],
["Shukr — bergan narsalari uchun Xudoga minnatdorlik bildirish demak. Iltijo — soʻrash demak — oʻz ehtiyojlaring uchun va boshqa odamlar uchun.", "Shukr — bergan narsalari uchun Khudoga minnatdorlik bildirish demak. Iltijo — sawrash demak — awz ehtiyojlaring uchun va boshqa odamlar uchun.", "Thanksgiving means thanking God for what he has given you. Supplication means asking — for your own needs and for other people.", "Philippians 4:6"],
["Isoning izdoshlari ham Xudoga sajda qiladi, lekin bu sen koʻrgan sajdadan boshqacha koʻrinishi mumkin. Biz Rabbiyga birga qoʻshiq aytib sajda qilamiz — va xuddi shunday, ishlab va butun hayotimizni Xudoni hurmatlaydigan tarzda yashab ham sajda qilamiz.", "Isoning izdoshlari ham Khudoga sajda qiladi, lekin bu sen kawrgan sajdadan boshqacha kawrinishi mumkin. Biz Rabbiyga birga qawshiq aytib sajda qilamiz — va khuddi shunday, ishlab va butun hayotimizni Khudoni hurmatlaydigan tarzda yashab ham sajda qilamiz.", "Followers of Jesus also worship God, but it may look different from worship you have seen elsewhere. We worship by singing to the Lord together — and just as much by working and living our whole lives in a way that honors God.", "Romans 12:1 · Colossians 3:23"]]},
{id:"obey",t:"Obedience",ne:"Itoat",art:FUZ_ART.obey,
note:["Xudo sevsin deb itoat qilmaysan. U allaqachon sevgani uchun itoat qilasan.", "Khudo sevsin deb itoat qilmaysan. U allaqachon sevgani uchun itoat qilasan.", "You do not obey so that God will love you. You obey because he already does."],
paras:[
["Isoga ergashish Uning taʼlimotini shunchaki bilish emas — unga itoat qilish demak. Iso soʻradi: nega Meni Rabbiy, Rabbiy deysizlar-u, aytganimni qilmaysizlar?", "Isoga ergashish Uning talimotini shunchaki bilish emas — unga itoat qilish demak. Iso sawradi: nega Meni Rabbiy, Rabbiy deysizlar-u, aytganimni qilmaysizlar?", "Following Jesus does not just mean knowing his teachings — it means obeying them. Jesus asked: why do you call me Lord, Lord, and do not do what I say?", "Luke 6:46"],
["Itoat qilish har doim oson emas. Eski odatlar va gunoh kuchli tortadi, va hech kim ularni oʻz kuchi bilan yenga olmaydi.", "Itoat qilish har doim oson emas. Eski odatlar va gunoh kuchli tortadi, va hech kim ularni awz kuchi bilan yenga olmaydi.", "Obeying is not always easy. Old habits and sin pull hard, and nobody can defeat them in their own strength."],
["Lekin xushxabar shu: Xudodan seni Oʻz Muqaddas Ruhi bilan toʻldirishini soʻrashing mumkin — va U senga Xudoga itoat qilish va gunohga yoʻq deyish uchun kuch beradi.", "Lekin khushkhabar shu: Khudodan seni Awz Muqaddas Ruhi bilan tawldirishini sawrashing mumkin — va U senga Khudoga itoat qilish va gunohga yawq deyish uchun kuch beradi.", "But here is the good news: you can ask God to fill you with his Holy Spirit — and he will empower you to obey God and to say no to sin.", "Titus 2:11–12 · Luke 11:13"],
["Qoqilganingda — Isoning har bir izdoshi baʼzida qoqiladi — Xudodan qochma. Unga tan ol, kechirimini qabul qil, oʻrningdan turib ergashishda davom et.", "Qoqilganingda — Isoning har bir izdoshi bazida qoqiladi — Khudodan qochma. Unga tan ol, kechirimini qabul qil, awrningdan turib ergashishda davom et.", "When you fail — and every follower of Jesus sometimes fails — do not run away from God. Confess it to him, receive his forgiveness, and get up and keep following.", "Proverbs 24:16 · 1 John 1:9"],
["Iso bu yoʻlni tor yoʻl deb atagan — lekin U bu yoʻlda sen bilan birga yuradi, va u hayotga olib boradi.", "Iso bu yawlni tor yawl deb atagan — lekin U bu yawlda sen bilan birga yuradi, va u hayotga olib boradi.", "Jesus called this way the narrow road — but he walks it with you, and it leads to life.", "Matthew 7:13–14 · Matthew 28:20"]]}]}
  ]
});
